IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cb5-nouns`
IMPORT `cb5-part19-investigation`
IMPORT `cb5-part19-1-damages`
IMPORT `cb5-part20-remedies`
IMPORT `cb5-part20-offences`
IMPORT `cb5-part20-1-electronic`
IMPORT `cb5-part21-notices`
IMPORT `cb5-part21-director`
IMPORT `cb5-part21-charter`
IMPORT `cb5-schedule-offences`
IMPORT `cb5-related-provisions`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), Parts XIX to XXI, the Schedule and the Related
-- Provisions -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. The text this was encoded from is a plain-text rendering of the Department of Justice
-- Canada consolidation current to 2026-09-30 (last amended 2026-03-26); it is not an official version,
-- and nothing here has been verified against the official text. Contains information licensed under
-- the Open Government Licence - Canada.
--
-- SEAT: a person who incorporates, directs or holds shares in a corporation under the Act (an
-- incorporator, a director or officer, or a shareholder, including a minority shareholder), asking what
-- the Act lets them do, what it requires of them, what they may require of the corporation, and what can be
-- done to them.
--
-- This layer phrases the rules of the modules imported above as the questions that person would ask. Nothing
-- here is new law, and no rule is restated: each question builds, in its WHERE, whatever record or choice the
-- module rule expects from the person's plain answers, and then calls that rule.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs: yes or no, a number, a date or a choice that the module
-- itself defines. Each has an @desc worded as the person would be asked. Where a module rule takes a party
-- (`Party`), the person is asked whether they are one of the kinds of party that matters, and the choice is
-- made in the WHERE. A judgment the Act hands to the court or to the Director ("it appears to the court that",
-- "the Director is satisfied that") is a question about that judgment: the person says whether the court or the
-- Director has made it, or would.
--
-- PAIRS (Hohfeld). Where a question is about what the person is owed (a claim), the paired question is about
-- what the other side must do or may do to the person; a power over the person is the person's liability.
-- Official duties appear only as what the person is owed or exposed to; there is no seat for an official.

§ `Canada Business Corporations Act, Parts XIX to XXI -- the questions of an incorporator, director, officer or shareholder`

§§ `Investigation (Part XIX)`

-- s 229(1). The applicants are a security holder or the Director; a person who holds no security of the
-- corporation, and is not the Director, is outside the section. "A court having jurisdiction in the place where
-- the corporation has its registered office" is the court asked.
@export May I apply to the court for an investigation of the corporation (s 229(1))?
GIVEN `I hold securities of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold securities of the corporation?
      `the court is in the place where the corporation has its registered office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court you would apply to the court with jurisdiction in the place where the corporation has its registered office?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I apply to the court for an investigation of the corporation` IF
    `may apply for an order directing an investigation within s 229(1)` applicant `the court is in the place where the corporation has its registered office`
    WHERE
        applicant MEANS IF `I hold securities of the corporation` THEN `a security holder` ELSE `any person`

-- s 229(2). The court may order an investigation of the corporation and its affiliates if, on an application
-- under s 229(1), it appears to the court that any one of four things is so.
@export May the court order an investigation of the corporation (s 229(2))?
GIVEN `an application has been made to the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an application for an investigation been made to the court?
      `it appears that the business of the corporation or an affiliate is or has been carried on with intent to defraud a person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the court that the business of the corporation or an affiliate is or has been carried on with intent to defraud any person?
      `it appears that the business or affairs, or the exercise of the directors' powers, is oppressive or unfairly prejudicial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the court that the business or affairs of the corporation or an affiliate are or have been carried on, or the directors' powers exercised, in a way that is oppressive or unfairly prejudicial to, or unfairly disregards the interests of, a security holder?
      `it appears that the corporation or an affiliate was formed or is to be dissolved for a fraudulent or unlawful purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the court that the corporation or an affiliate was formed, or is to be dissolved, for a fraudulent or unlawful purpose?
      `it appears that persons concerned with the corporation have acted fraudulently or dishonestly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the court that persons concerned with the formation, business or affairs of the corporation or an affiliate have acted fraudulently or dishonestly in connection with them?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the court order an investigation of the corporation` IF
    `the court may order an investigation within s 229(2)` `an application has been made to the court` `it appears that the business of the corporation or an affiliate is or has been carried on with intent to defraud a person` `it appears that the business or affairs, or the exercise of the directors' powers, is oppressive or unfairly prejudicial` `it appears that the corporation or an affiliate was formed or is to be dissolved for a fraudulent or unlawful purpose` `it appears that persons concerned with the corporation have acted fraudulently or dishonestly`

-- s 229(3). The duty is the security holder's; the Director holds the correlative claim, and may appear. The
-- paired question after this one is what the Director may do on my application.
@export Must I give the Director notice of my application for an investigation (s 229(3))?
GIVEN `I hold securities of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold securities of the corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I give the Director notice of my application for an investigation` IF
    `the applicant must give the Director reasonable notice within s 229(3)` applicant
    WHERE
        applicant MEANS IF `I hold securities of the corporation` THEN `a security holder` ELSE `any person`

@export Have I complied with my duty to give the Director notice of my application for an investigation (s 229(3))?
GIVEN `I hold securities of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold securities of the corporation?
      `the Director was given reasonable notice of my application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the Director given reasonable notice of your application?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I complied with my duty to give the Director notice of my application for an investigation` IF
    `the applicant has complied with the duty to notify the Director within s 229(3)` applicant `the Director was given reasonable notice of my application`
    WHERE
        applicant MEANS IF `I hold securities of the corporation` THEN `a security holder` ELSE `any person`

@export Is the Director entitled to appear and be heard on my application for an investigation (s 229(3))?
GIVEN `I am a security holder who has made an application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a security holder who has made an application for an investigation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the Director entitled to appear and be heard on my application for an investigation` IF
    `the Director is entitled to appear and be heard within s 229(3)` `I am a security holder who has made an application`

-- s 229(4), (5), (6).
@export Must I give security for costs on my application for an investigation (s 229(4))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I give security for costs on my application for an investigation` IF
    `an applicant under s 229 is required to give security for costs within s 229(4)`

@export Must my application for an investigation be heard in camera (s 229(5))?
GIVEN `my application is made ex parte` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your application made ex parte, that is, without notice to the corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my application for an investigation be heard in camera` IF
    `the application must be heard in camera within s 229(5)` `my application is made ex parte`

@export May I publish something about ex parte proceedings for an investigation (s 229(6))?
GIVEN `the proceedings are ex parte proceedings for an investigation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings ex parte proceedings under the investigation section?
      `the court has authorized the publication` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court authorized you to publish it?
      `the corporation being investigated has consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation being investigated consented in writing to the publication?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I publish something about ex parte proceedings for an investigation` IF
    `publishing anything relating to the proceedings is permitted within s 229(6)` `the proceedings are ex parte proceedings for an investigation` `the court has authorized the publication` `the corporation being investigated has consented in writing`

-- s 230(1). "Any order it thinks fit including ...": the listed kinds and any other.
@export May the court make this kind of order in an investigation of the corporation (s 230(1))?
GIVEN `the kind of order` IS A `Kind of order in connection with an investigation (s 230(1))` @desc Which kind of order is in question? (the listed kinds are those in section 230(1)(a) to (l); the last choice stands for any other order)
      `the order is made in connection with an investigation under Part XIX` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order made in connection with an investigation ordered under the investigation Part?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the court make this kind of order in an investigation of the corporation` IF
    `the court may make an order of the kind within s 230(1)` `the kind of order` `the order is made in connection with an investigation under Part XIX`

-- s 231(1), (2). What the inspector may do: only what the order sets out, and, besides that, share what it learns with
-- a public official who is investigating the same matter.
@export Can the inspector use this power over me (s 231(1))?
GIVEN `the power is set out in the order appointing the inspector` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the power set out in the order that appointed the inspector?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the inspector use this power over me` IF
    `an inspector has the power within s 231(1)` `the power is set out in the order appointing the inspector`

@export May the inspector pass what I told them on to another public official (s 231(2))?
GIVEN `the inspector was appointed to investigate a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the inspector appointed to investigate a corporation?
      `the recipient is a public official in Canada or elsewhere authorized to exercise investigatory powers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person who would receive it a public official, in Canada or elsewhere, authorized to exercise investigatory powers?
      `the recipient is investigating the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the recipient investigating the corporation?
      `the recipient is investigating the same or similar improper conduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the recipient investigating an allegation of improper conduct that is the same as or similar to the conduct described in the section on the grounds for an investigation (subsection 229(2))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the inspector pass what I told them on to another public official` IF
    `an inspector may furnish information to or exchange it with the official within s 231(2)` `the inspector was appointed to investigate a corporation` `the recipient is a public official in Canada or elsewhere authorized to exercise investigatory powers` `the recipient is investigating the corporation` `the recipient is investigating the same or similar improper conduct`

-- s 231(3). My claim against the inspector.
@export Am I entitled to a copy of the order that appointed the inspector (s 231(3))?
GIVEN `I am an interested person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an interested person in the investigation?
      `I have asked the inspector for a copy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you asked the inspector for a copy?
      `the order was made under subsection 230(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the order made under the court's power to order an investigation (section 230(1))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to a copy of the order that appointed the inspector` IF
    `the inspector must produce a copy of the order within s 231(3)` `I am an interested person` `I have asked the inspector for a copy` `the order was made under subsection 230(1)`

-- s 232(1), (2).
@export May I apply to the court for an in camera hearing and directions (s 232(1))?
GIVEN `I am an interested person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an interested person in the investigation?
      `the hearing is conducted by an inspector under Part XIX` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the hearing conducted by an inspector appointed in the investigation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I apply to the court for an in camera hearing and directions` IF
    `an interested person may apply to the court for an in camera hearing and directions within s 232(1)` `I am an interested person` `the hearing is conducted by an inspector under Part XIX`

@export Do I have a right to be represented by counsel at the inspector's hearing (s 232(2))?
GIVEN `my conduct is being investigated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your conduct being investigated?
      `I am being examined at the hearing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you being examined at a hearing conducted by an inspector?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I have a right to be represented by counsel at the inspector's hearing` IF
    `the person has a right to be represented by counsel within s 232(2)` `my conduct is being investigated` `I am being examined at the hearing`

-- s 233 (two sentences of one section: no excuse, and a bar on later use).
@export Am I excused from giving evidence to an inspector because it may incriminate me (s 233)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I excused from giving evidence to an inspector because it may incriminate me` IF
    `a person is excused from giving evidence by reason only that it tends to criminate within s 233`

@export Can what I tell an inspector be used against me later (s 233)?
GIVEN `I gave the evidence to an inspector, and it tends to criminate me or expose me to a proceeding or penalty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give the evidence to an inspector in an investigation, and does it tend to criminate you or subject you to a proceeding or penalty?
      `the proceeding was instituted against me after I gave the evidence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the proceeding instituted against you after you gave the evidence?
      `the proceeding is under an Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proceeding one under an Act of Parliament?
      `the proceeding is a prosecution for perjury in giving the evidence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proceeding a prosecution under section 132 of the Criminal Code for perjury in giving the evidence?
      `the proceeding is a prosecution under section 136 of the Criminal Code in respect of the evidence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proceeding a prosecution under section 136 of the Criminal Code in respect of the evidence?
GIVETH A `Use of evidence given to an inspector (s 233)`
DECIDE `Can what I tell an inspector be used against me later` IS
    `the use of the evidence within s 233` `I gave the evidence to an inspector, and it tends to criminate me or expose me to a proceeding or penalty` `the proceeding was instituted against me after I gave the evidence` `the proceeding is under an Act of Parliament` `the proceeding is a prosecution for perjury in giving the evidence` `the proceeding is a prosecution under section 136 of the Criminal Code in respect of the evidence`

-- s 234. My immunity: absolute privilege.
@export Am I protected by absolute privilege for what I say or write in an investigation (s 234)?
GIVEN `the statement or report was made in an investigation under Part XIX` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the oral or written statement or report made in an investigation under the investigation Part?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I protected by absolute privilege for what I say or write in an investigation` IF
    `the statement or report has absolute privilege within s 234` `the statement or report was made in an investigation under Part XIX`

-- s 235. The Director's power over me, and my duty (the pair), then the offence.
@export Can the Director require me to report who owns or controls a security (s 235(1))?
GIVEN `the Director is satisfied that there is reason to inquire into the ownership or control of a security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Director satisfied that there is reason to inquire into the ownership or control of a security of a corporation or its affiliates, for the purposes of the Act's insider trading, shareholder or acquisition Parts or of enforcing a regulation under section 174?
      `the Director reasonably believes I have or had an interest or right in the security, or act or acted for someone who has` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Director reasonably believe that you have or had an interest or right in the security, or that you act or acted on behalf of a person who has one?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Director require me to report who owns or controls a security` IF
    `the Director may require the person to report within s 235(1)` `the Director is satisfied that there is reason to inquire into the ownership or control of a security` `the Director reasonably believes I have or had an interest or right in the security, or act or acted for someone who has`

@export Have I made the report the Director required of me (s 235(1))?
GIVEN `I reported the information I have or can reasonably be expected to obtain about present and past interests or rights in the security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you report the information you have, or can reasonably be expected to obtain, about present and past interests or rights in the security?
      `I reported the names and addresses of the persons with such an interest or right and of anyone acting for them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you report the names and addresses of the persons with such an interest or right, and of any person who acts or has acted for them in relation to the security?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I made the report the Director required of me` IF
    `the person has made the report required within s 235(1)` `I reported the information I have or can reasonably be expected to obtain about present and past interests or rights in the security` `I reported the names and addresses of the persons with such an interest or right and of anyone acting for them`

@export Am I deemed to have an interest or right in a security (s 235(2))?
GIVEN `I have a right to vote or to acquire or dispose of the security or any interest in it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a right to vote, or to acquire or dispose of, the security or any interest or right in it?
      `my consent is necessary for others to exercise rights or privileges attached to the security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your consent necessary for the exercise of the rights or privileges of another person with an interest or right in the security?
      `others with an interest in the security are required or accustomed to act on my instructions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can another person with an interest or right in the security be required, or are they accustomed, to exercise the rights or privileges attached to it in accordance with your instructions?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I deemed to have an interest or right in a security` IF
    `the person is deemed to have an interest or right in the security within s 235(2)` `I have a right to vote or to acquire or dispose of the security or any interest in it` `my consent is necessary for others to exercise rights or privileges attached to the security` `others with an interest in the security are required or accustomed to act on my instructions`

@export Will the Director publish the particulars I reported (s 235(3))?
GIVEN `the particulars were obtained by the Director under section 235` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the particulars obtained by the Director under the ownership and control section?
      `the particulars are required to be disclosed by the Act or the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Act or a regulation require the particulars to be disclosed?
      `the particulars have not previously been disclosed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the particulars not previously been so disclosed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will the Director publish the particulars I reported` IF
    `the Director must publish the particulars within s 235(3)` `the particulars were obtained by the Director under section 235` `the particulars are required to be disclosed by the Act or the regulations` `the particulars have not previously been disclosed`

@export Am I guilty of an offence if I do not give the report the Director requires (s 235(4))?
GIVEN `a requirement was made of me under subsection 235(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a requirement made of you under the ownership and control section?
      `I complied with the requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you comply with it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I guilty of an offence if I do not give the report the Director requires` IF
    `the person is guilty of an offence within s 235(4)` `a requirement was made of me under subsection 235(1)` `I complied with the requirement`

@export What is the largest fine I could face for failing to give the report (dollars) (s 235(4))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the largest fine I could face for failing to give the report` IS
    (`the most the court may impose within s 235(4)`)'s `largest fine in dollars`

@export What is the longest imprisonment I could face for failing to give the report (months) (s 235(4))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the longest imprisonment I could face for failing to give the report` IS
    (`the most the court may impose within s 235(4)`)'s `longest imprisonment in months`

@export As a director or officer, am I guilty when my body corporate fails to give the report (s 235(5))?
GIVEN `the body corporate commits an offence under subsection 235(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the body corporate committed the offence of failing to comply with the ownership and control section?
      `I am a director or officer of the body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director or officer of the body corporate?
      `I knowingly authorized, permitted or acquiesced in the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you knowingly authorize, permit or acquiesce in the commission of the offence?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As a director or officer, am I guilty when my body corporate fails to give the report` IF
    `the director or officer is a party to and guilty of the offence within s 235(5)` `the body corporate commits an offence under subsection 235(4)` `I am a director or officer of the body corporate` `I knowingly authorized, permitted or acquiesced in the offence`

@export What is the largest fine I could face as a director or officer who authorized the failure to report (dollars) (s 235(5))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the largest fine I could face as a director or officer who authorized the failure to report` IS
    (`the most the court may impose on a director or officer within s 235(5)`)'s `largest fine in dollars`

@export What is the longest imprisonment I could face as a director or officer who authorized the failure to report (months) (s 235(5))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the longest imprisonment I could face as a director or officer who authorized the failure to report` IS
    (`the most the court may impose on a director or officer within s 235(5)`)'s `longest imprisonment in months`

-- s 236, s 237.
@export Does the investigation Part take away my solicitor-client privilege (s 236)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the investigation Part take away my solicitor-client privilege` IF
    `Part XIX affects solicitor-client privilege or professional secrecy within s 236`

@export Can the Director make inquiries of me and require records (s 237(1))?
GIVEN `the inquiry relates to compliance with the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the inquiry relate to compliance with the Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Director make inquiries of me and require records` IF
    `the Director may make the inquiry and require records within s 237(1)` `the inquiry relates to compliance with the Act`

@export Have I complied with my duty to respond to the Director's inquiry (s 237(2))?
GIVEN `an inquiry was made of me under subsection 237(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Director make an inquiry of you?
      `I responded to the inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you respond to it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I complied with my duty to respond to the Director's inquiry` IF
    `the person has complied with the duty to respond within s 237(2)` `an inquiry was made of me under subsection 237(1)` `I responded to the inquiry`

§§ `Apportioning an award of damages (Part XIX.1)`

-- s 237.1. The Part's own words: the plaintiff's "financial interest", the "financial loss", and a "third party".
@export Is what I hold a financial interest for the apportionment Part (s 237.1)?
GIVEN `the kind of financial interest` IS A `Kind of financial interest (s 237.1)` @desc Which kind of holding is it? (a security; a title to or interest in capital, assets, property, profits, earnings or royalties; an option or subscription; an agreement valuing the interest by a portfolio of assets; an agreement to repay money or treat it as a subscription; a profit-sharing agreement; a lease, claim or royalty in oil, gas or mining; an income or annuity contract; an investment contract; anything prescribed; or none of these)
      `it is a financial interest in the ordinary meaning of the words` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a financial interest in the ordinary meaning of the words?
      `the income or annuity contract was issued by an insurance company governed by an Act of Parliament or a law of a province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is an income or annuity contract: was it issued by an insurance company governed by an Act of Parliament or a law of a province?
      `it is prescribed by the regulations to be a financial interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the regulations prescribe it to be a financial interest?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is what I hold a financial interest for the apportionment Part` IF
    `financial interest within s 237.1` `the kind of financial interest` `it is a financial interest in the ordinary meaning of the words` `the income or annuity contract was issued by an insurance company governed by an Act of Parliament or a law of a province` `it is prescribed by the regulations to be a financial interest`

@export Is my loss a financial loss for the apportionment Part (s 237.1)?
GIVEN `it is a financial loss` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a financial loss?
      `it arose out of an error, omission or misstatement in financial information concerning a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it arise out of an error, omission or misstatement in financial information concerning a corporation?
      `the financial information is required under this Act or the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the financial information required under the Act or the regulations?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my loss a financial loss for the apportionment Part` IF
    `financial loss within s 237.1` `it is a financial loss` `it arose out of an error, omission or misstatement in financial information concerning a corporation` `the financial information is required under this Act or the regulations`

@export Am I a third party for the apportionment Part (s 237.1)?
GIVEN `I am a third party in the ordinary meaning of the words` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a third party in the ordinary meaning of the words?
      `I am a subsequent party joined in proceedings before a court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a subsequent party that is joined in proceedings before a court?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a third party for the apportionment Part` IF
    `third party within s 237.1` `I am a third party in the ordinary meaning of the words` `I am a subsequent party joined in proceedings before a court`

-- s 237.2 with S.C. 2001, c. 14, s. 233. The Part reaches an award of damages for financial loss where more than
-- one defendant or third party is found responsible, unless the plaintiff is of an excluded kind, and does not
-- reach a proceeding begun before section 115 of the 2001 Act came into force.
@export Does the apportionment Part govern the damages awarded in my claim (s 237.2; S.C. 2001, c. 14, s. 233)?
GIVEN `damages are awarded to a plaintiff for financial loss` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are damages awarded to a plaintiff for financial loss?
      `the number of defendants and third parties found responsible` IS A NUMBER @desc How many defendants and third parties has the court found responsible for the financial loss?
      `the kind of plaintiff` IS A `Kind of plaintiff (s 237.2(2))` @desc Which kind of plaintiff is it? (the Crown, an agent of the Crown or a Crown corporation, a charity or foundation, an unsecured creditor for goods or services, or any other plaintiff)
      `a substantial part of the plaintiff's activities involves trading in securities or other financial instruments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a substantial part of the plaintiff's activities involve trading, including making investments in, securities or other financial instruments?
      `the day the proceeding was commenced` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the proceeding commenced?
      `the day section 115 of the 2001 amending Act came into force` IS A DATE @desc On what day did section 115 of S.C. 2001, c. 14 (which enacted the apportionment Part) come into force?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the apportionment Part govern the damages awarded in my claim` IF
    `Part XIX.1 governs the apportionment of the damages` `damages are awarded to a plaintiff for financial loss` `the number of defendants and third parties found responsible` `the kind of plaintiff` `a substantial part of the plaintiff's activities involves trading in securities or other financial instruments` `the day the proceeding was commenced` `the day section 115 of the 2001 amending Act came into force`

-- s 237.3(1). A defendant is liable only for the portion that matches their degree of responsibility.
@export How much of the damages am I liable for as a defendant (dollars) (s 237.3(1))?
GIVEN `the damages awarded in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc How much in damages has the court awarded to the plaintiff, in dollars?
      `my degree of responsibility as a fraction of the loss` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your degree of responsibility for the loss, as a fraction from 0 to 1 (for 40 per cent, 0.4)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of the damages am I liable for as a defendant` IS
    `the portion of the damages for which a defendant or third party is liable within s 237.3(1)` `the damages awarded in dollars` `my degree of responsibility as a fraction of the loss`

-- s 237.3(2). The plaintiff's power to ask the court to reallocate: its time limit, and whether it may be used.
@export By what day may the plaintiff apply to reallocate an uncollectable amount (s 237.3(2))?
GIVEN `the day the judgment was made enforceable` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the judgment made enforceable?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day may the plaintiff apply to reallocate an uncollectable amount` IS
    `the last day to apply to reallocate an uncollectable amount within s 237.3(2)` `the day the judgment was made enforceable`

@export May the court reallocate an uncollectable amount to me as another responsible defendant (s 237.3(2))?
GIVEN `part of the damages against a responsible defendant or third party is uncollectable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is part of the damages awarded against a responsible defendant or third party uncollectable?
      `the plaintiff has applied for the reallocation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the plaintiff applied for the reallocation?
      `the day the judgment was made enforceable` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the judgment made enforceable?
      `the day of the application` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the application made?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the court reallocate an uncollectable amount to me as another responsible defendant` IF
    `the court may reallocate the uncollectable amount within s 237.3(2)` `part of the damages against a responsible defendant or third party is uncollectable` `the plaintiff has applied for the reallocation` `the day the judgment was made enforceable` `the day of the application`

-- s 237.3(3), (4). My exposure: the uncollectable amount times my share of the whole loss, but never more than
-- half of what was originally awarded against me.
@export What is the most that can be reallocated to me (dollars) (s 237.3(3), (4))?
GIVEN `the uncollectable amount in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of the damages is uncollectable, in dollars?
      `my degree of responsibility for the total financial loss as a fraction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your degree of responsibility for the total financial loss, as a fraction from 0 to 1?
      `the amount originally awarded against me in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc How much was originally awarded against you, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most that can be reallocated to me` IS
    `the most that may be reallocated to that defendant or third party within s 237.3(4)` `the amount reallocated before the cap` `the amount originally awarded against me in dollars`
    WHERE
        `the amount reallocated before the cap` MEANS `the amount that may be reallocated to the other defendant or third party within s 237.3(3)` `the uncollectable amount in dollars` `my degree of responsibility for the total financial loss as a fraction`

-- s 237.4.
@export Can the plaintiff recover the whole of the damages from me because I acted fraudulently or dishonestly (s 237.4(1))?
GIVEN `I have been held responsible for the financial loss` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been held responsible for the financial loss?
      `it was established that I acted fraudulently or dishonestly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it established that you acted fraudulently or dishonestly?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the plaintiff recover the whole of the damages from me because I acted fraudulently or dishonestly` IF
    `the plaintiff may recover the whole amount of the damages from the defendant or third party within s 237.4(1)` `I have been held responsible for the financial loss` `it was established that I acted fraudulently or dishonestly`

@export Am I entitled to claim contribution from the other defendants after a fraud finding against me (s 237.4(2))?
GIVEN `I am the defendant or third party who must pay the whole amount for fraud or dishonesty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the defendant or third party from whom the whole amount may be recovered because of fraud or dishonesty?
      `the other defendant or third party is held responsible for the loss` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the other defendant or third party held responsible for the loss?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to claim contribution from the other defendants after a fraud finding against me` IF
    `the defendant or third party is entitled to claim contribution within s 237.4(2)` `I am the defendant or third party who must pay the whole amount for fraud or dishonesty` `the other defendant or third party is held responsible for the loss`

-- s 237.5(1), (1.1), (2). The plaintiff's claim to hold the defendants jointly and severally liable. The record of
-- close-of-business positions the module rule reads is built here from one acquisition at most.
@export Are the defendants jointly and severally liable to me as an investor (s 237.5)?
GIVEN `the defendants and third parties are those referred to in subsection 237.2(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the defendants and third parties those the court has found responsible for the same financial loss, as in the apportionment section?
      `I am an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an individual?
      `I am a personal body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a personal body corporate (a body corporate not actively engaged in a financial, commercial or industrial business and controlled by an individual or by a group of relatives)?
      `I had a financial interest in the corporation on the day of the error` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a financial interest in the corporation on the day the error, omission or misstatement occurred?
      `the day the error occurred` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the error, omission or misstatement occur?
      `the day it was generally disclosed` IS A DATE @desc On what day, as the court determines, was it generally disclosed?
      `I acquired a financial interest in the corporation in that period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you acquire a financial interest in the corporation between those two days?
      `the day I acquired it` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you acquire it?
      `my total financial interest at the close of that day, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the value of your total financial interest in the corporation at the close of business on that day, in dollars?
      `I have established the value of my total financial interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you established the value of your total financial interest?
      `my total financial interest on the day of the error, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the value of your total financial interest in the corporation at the close of business on the day of the error, in dollars?
      `the prescribed amount in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the prescribed amount, in dollars? (it is fixed by the regulations)
      `I bring the action as a member of a partnership or other association` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you bring the action as a member of a partnership or other association?
      `I bring the action as a trustee in bankruptcy, liquidator, receiver or sequestrator of a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you bring the action as a trustee in bankruptcy, liquidator, receiver or sequestrator of a body corporate?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are the defendants jointly and severally liable to me as an investor` IF
    `the defendants and third parties are jointly and severally liable within s 237.5(1)` `the defendants and third parties are those referred to in subsection 237.2(1)` `I am an individual` `I am a personal body corporate` `I had a financial interest in the corporation on the day of the error` `the day the error occurred` `the day it was generally disclosed` positions `I have established the value of my total financial interest` `my total financial interest on the day of the error, in dollars` `the prescribed amount in dollars` excluded
    WHERE
        excluded MEANS `subsection 237.5(1) does not apply to the plaintiff within s 237.5(1.1)` `I bring the action as a member of a partnership or other association` `I bring the action as a trustee in bankruptcy, liquidator, receiver or sequestrator of a body corporate`
        positions MEANS IF `I acquired a financial interest in the corporation in that period`
                        THEN LIST `Close of business position of a plaintiff (s 237.5(1))` WITH
                                      `the day` IS `the day I acquired it`
                                      `the plaintiff acquired a financial interest on that day` IS TRUE
                                      `value of the plaintiff's total financial interest in the corporation in dollars` IS `my total financial interest at the close of that day, in dollars`
                        ELSE EMPTY

@export Is my body corporate a personal body corporate (s 237.5(2)(a))?
GIVEN `my body corporate is not actively engaged in any financial, commercial or industrial business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your body corporate not actively engaged in any financial, commercial or industrial business?
      `my body corporate is controlled by an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it controlled by an individual?
      `my body corporate is controlled by a group of individuals connected by marriage, common-law partnership or a legal parent-child relationship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it controlled by a group of individuals connected by marriage, common-law partnership or any legal parent-child relationship, or connected indirectly by a combination of those relationships?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my body corporate a personal body corporate` IF
    `personal body corporate within s 237.5(2)(a)` `my body corporate is not actively engaged in any financial, commercial or industrial business` `my body corporate is controlled by an individual` `my body corporate is controlled by a group of individuals connected by marriage, common-law partnership or a legal parent-child relationship`

@export Am I in a common-law partnership with this person for the apportionment Part (s 237.5(2)(b))?
GIVEN `we are cohabiting with each other in a conjugal relationship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you and the other person cohabiting with each other in a conjugal relationship?
      `the number of years we have cohabited` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many years have you cohabited?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I in a common-law partnership with this person for the apportionment Part` IF
    `common-law partnership within s 237.5(2)(b)` `we are cohabiting with each other in a conjugal relationship` `the number of years we have cohabited`

-- s 237.6(1). Above the prescribed amount the court may still hold them jointly and severally liable.
@export May the court hold the defendants jointly and severally liable to me even though my holding is above the prescribed amount (s 237.6)?
GIVEN `the value of my total financial interest in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of your total financial interest, in dollars?
      `the prescribed amount in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the prescribed amount, in dollars? (it is fixed by the regulations)
      `the court considers it just and reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court consider that it is just and reasonable to hold the defendants and third parties jointly and severally liable?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the court hold the defendants jointly and severally liable to me even though my holding is above the prescribed amount` IF
    `the court may hold the defendants and third parties jointly and severally liable within s 237.6(1)` `the value of my total financial interest in dollars` `the prescribed amount in dollars` `the court considers it just and reasonable`

-- ss 237.3(1), 237.4(1), 237.5(1), 237.6(1) together: on what footing a defendant or third party answers for the damages.
@export On what basis am I liable for the damages awarded (s 237.3(1), s 237.4 to s 237.6)?
GIVEN `the plaintiff may recover the whole amount from me for fraud or dishonesty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Under the fraud-or-dishonesty section, may the plaintiff recover the whole amount of the damages from you?
      `the defendants and third parties are jointly and severally liable to the plaintiff as an investor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Under the investor section, are the defendants and third parties jointly and severally liable to the plaintiff?
      `the court has held us jointly and severally liable on equitable grounds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court held the defendants and third parties jointly and severally liable because it considered it just and reasonable?
GIVETH A `Basis of the liability of a defendant or third party (Part XIX.1)`
DECIDE `On what basis am I liable for the damages awarded` IS
    `the basis of the liability within s 237.3(1) and s 237.4 to s 237.6` `the plaintiff may recover the whole amount from me for fraud or dishonesty` `the defendants and third parties are jointly and severally liable to the plaintiff as an investor` `the court has held us jointly and severally liable on equitable grounds`

-- s 237.7(1). The value of a security traded on an organized market. Each price is asked as a yes/no and a number.
@export What is the value of my security for the apportionment Part (dollars) (s 237.7)?
GIVEN `the security is traded on an organized market` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the security traded on an organized market (a recognized exchange, or a market that regularly publishes the price of that class in a publication generally available to the public)?
      `a closing price was given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a closing price for that class of security on the day?
      `the closing price in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the closing price, in dollars? (any number if none was given)
      `highest and lowest prices were given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there highest and lowest prices for that class of security on the day?
      `the highest price in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the highest price, in dollars? (any number if none was given)
      `the lowest price in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the lowest price, in dollars? (any number if none was given)
      `the security was traded on the day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the security traded on the day?
      `bid and ask prices were given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there bid and ask prices for that class of security on the day?
      `the bid price in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the bid price, in dollars? (any number if none was given)
      `the ask price in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the ask price, in dollars? (any number if none was given)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the value of my security for the apportionment Part` IS
    `the value of the security within s 237.7(1)` `the security is traded on an organized market` closing highest lowest `the security was traded on the day` bid ask
    WHERE
        closing MEANS IF `a closing price was given` THEN JUST `the closing price in dollars` ELSE NOTHING
        highest MEANS IF `highest and lowest prices were given` THEN JUST `the highest price in dollars` ELSE NOTHING
        lowest MEANS IF `highest and lowest prices were given` THEN JUST `the lowest price in dollars` ELSE NOTHING
        bid MEANS IF `bid and ask prices were given` THEN JUST `the bid price in dollars` ELSE NOTHING
        ask MEANS IF `bid and ask prices were given` THEN JUST `the ask price in dollars` ELSE NOTHING

@export May the court adjust the value of my security (s 237.7(2))?
GIVEN `the court considers it reasonable to adjust the value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court consider it reasonable to adjust the value of the security?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the court adjust the value of my security` IF
    `the court may adjust the value within s 237.7(2)` `the court considers it reasonable to adjust the value`

@export As of what day is the value of my security determined (s 237.7(3))?
GIVEN `the day the error occurred` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the error, omission or misstatement occur?
      `the day it was generally disclosed` IS A DATE @desc On what day, as the court determines, was it generally disclosed?
      `I acquired the security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you acquire the security after the error occurred?
      `the day I acquired the security` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you acquire it? (any date if you did not)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `As of what day is the value of my security determined` IS
    `the day as of which the value is determined within s 237.7(3)` `the day the error occurred` `the day it was generally disclosed` acquired
    WHERE
        acquired MEANS IF `I acquired the security` THEN JUST `the day I acquired the security` ELSE NOTHING

@export Is this an organized market for my security (s 237.7(4))?
GIVEN `it is a recognized exchange for a class of securities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a recognized exchange for the class of securities?
      `it is a market that regularly publishes the price of that class of securities in a publication generally available to the public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a market that regularly publishes the price of that class of securities in a publication generally available to the public?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this an organized market for my security` IF
    `organized market within s 237.7(4)` `it is a recognized exchange for a class of securities` `it is a market that regularly publishes the price of that class of securities in a publication generally available to the public`

@export Must the court determine the value of my financial interest itself (s 237.8(1))?
GIVEN `the financial interest is subject to resale restrictions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the financial interest subject to resale restrictions?
      `there is no organized market for the financial interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there no organized market for the financial interest?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the court determine the value of my financial interest itself` IF
    `the court must determine the value within s 237.8(1)` `the financial interest is subject to resale restrictions` `there is no organized market for the financial interest`

@export May I ask the court to determine the value of my financial interest (s 237.9)?
GIVEN `my application is made before or during the course of the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your application made before or during the course of the proceedings?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I ask the court to determine the value of my financial interest` IF
    `the plaintiff may apply for the court to determine the value of the financial interest within s 237.9` `my application is made before or during the course of the proceedings`

§§ `Remedies (Part XX)`

-- s 238. A complainant is one of four kinds of person; the fourth is the court's own discretion.
@export Am I a complainant who may use the remedies Part (s 238)?
GIVEN `I am or was a registered holder or beneficial owner of a security of the corporation or an affiliate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you, or were you, a registered holder or beneficial owner of a security of the corporation or any of its affiliates?
      `I am or was a director or officer of the corporation or an affiliate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you, or were you, a director or officer of the corporation or any of its affiliates?
      `I am the Director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the Director appointed under the Act?
      `the court finds me a proper person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court, in its discretion, find you a proper person to make an application under the remedies Part?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a complainant who may use the remedies Part` IF
    `complainant within s 238` `I am or was a registered holder or beneficial owner of a security of the corporation or an affiliate` `I am or was a director or officer of the corporation or an affiliate` `I am the Director` `the court finds me a proper person`

@export Is this an action under the remedies Part (s 238)?
GIVEN `it is an action under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an action under the Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this an action under the remedies Part` IF
    `action within s 238` `it is an action under this Act`

-- s 239. Leave to bring or take over an action for the corporation (a derivative action).
@export May I apply to the court for leave to bring an action in the corporation's name (s 239(1))?
GIVEN `I am a complainant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a complainant (a current or former security holder, a current or former director or officer, the Director, or a person the court finds proper)?
      `my application is for leave to bring or intervene in an action for the corporation or its subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your application for leave to bring an action in the name and on behalf of the corporation or a subsidiary, or to intervene in an action to which either is a party?
      `my purpose is to prosecute, defend or discontinue the action for the body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your purpose to prosecute, defend or discontinue the action on behalf of the body corporate?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I apply to the court for leave to bring an action in the corporation's name` IF
    `a complainant may apply to a court for leave to act for the corporation within s 239(1)` `I am a complainant` `my application is for leave to bring or intervene in an action for the corporation or its subsidiary` `my purpose is to prosecute, defend or discontinue the action for the body corporate`

@export Have I given the directors enough notice before applying for leave (s 239(2)(a))?
GIVEN `the day I gave the directors notice of my intention to apply` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you give the directors notice of your intention to apply to the court?
      `the day I make my application` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you bring the application?
      `the court ordered a different notice period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court ordered a different notice period?
      `the directors do not bring, diligently prosecute or defend or discontinue the action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the directors fail to bring, diligently prosecute or defend, or discontinue the action?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I given the directors enough notice before applying for leave` IF
    `the condition of notice to the directors is met within s 239(2)(a)` `the day I gave the directors notice of my intention to apply` `the day I make my application` `the court ordered a different notice period` `the directors do not bring, diligently prosecute or defend or discontinue the action`

@export May the court let the action be brought for the corporation (s 239(2))?
GIVEN `the court is satisfied that the notice condition is met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that notice was given to the directors as the Act requires?
      `the court is satisfied that I am acting in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that you are acting in good faith?
      `the court is satisfied that it appears to be in the interests of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that it appears to be in the interests of the corporation or its subsidiary that the action be brought, prosecuted, defended or discontinued?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the court let the action be brought for the corporation` IF
    `the action may be brought or the intervention made within s 239(2)` `the court is satisfied that the notice condition is met` `the court is satisfied that I am acting in good faith` `the court is satisfied that it appears to be in the interests of the corporation`

@export May the court make this kind of order in a derivative action (s 240)?
GIVEN `the kind of order` IS A `Kind of order in a derivative action (s 240)` @desc Which kind of order is in question? (the listed kinds are in section 240(a) to (d); the last choice stands for any other order)
      `the order is made in connection with an action brought or intervened in under section 239` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order made in connection with an action brought, or intervened in, with the court's leave?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the court make this kind of order in a derivative action` IF
    `the court may make an order of the kind within s 240` `the kind of order` `the order is made in connection with an action brought or intervened in under section 239`

-- s 241. The oppression remedy.
@export May I apply to the court for relief from oppression (s 241(1))?
GIVEN `I am a complainant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a complainant (a current or former security holder, a current or former director or officer, the Director, or a person the court finds proper)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I apply to the court for relief from oppression` IF
    `a complainant may apply to a court for an order within s 241(1)` `I am a complainant`

@export May the court make an order to rectify what I complain of as oppressive (s 241(2))?
GIVEN `I have applied under subsection 241(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you applied to the court for relief from oppression?
      `the court is satisfied that an act or omission of the corporation or an affiliate effects a result` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that an act or omission of the corporation or an affiliate effects a result complained of?
      `the court is satisfied that the business or affairs are or have been carried on in a manner complained of` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that the business or affairs of the corporation or an affiliate are or have been carried on or conducted in a manner complained of?
      `the court is satisfied that the directors' powers are or have been exercised in a manner complained of` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that the powers of the directors of the corporation or an affiliate are or have been exercised in a manner complained of?
      `the result or manner is oppressive or unfairly prejudicial to or unfairly disregards the interests of the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the result or manner oppressive or unfairly prejudicial to, or does it unfairly disregard, the interests of a security holder, creditor, director or officer?
      `I am a security holder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a security holder, creditor, director or officer whose interests are affected? (answer yes if you hold securities)
      `I am a creditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a creditor whose interests are affected?
      `I am a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director whose interests are affected?
      `I am an officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer whose interests are affected?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the court make an order to rectify what I complain of as oppressive` IF
    `the court may make an order to rectify the matters complained of within s 241(2)` `I have applied under subsection 241(1)` `the court is satisfied that an act or omission of the corporation or an affiliate effects a result` `the court is satisfied that the business or affairs are or have been carried on in a manner complained of` `the court is satisfied that the directors' powers are or have been exercised in a manner complained of` `the result or manner is oppressive or unfairly prejudicial to or unfairly disregards the interests of the person` party
    WHERE
        party MEANS IF `I am a security holder` THEN `a security holder`
                    ELSE IF `I am a creditor` THEN `a creditor`
                          ELSE IF `I am a director` THEN `a director`
                                ELSE IF `I am an officer` THEN `an officer`
                                      ELSE `any person`

@export May the court make this kind of order on my oppression application (s 241(3))?
GIVEN `the kind of order` IS A `Kind of order on an application for relief from oppression (s 241(3))` @desc Which kind of order is in question? (the listed kinds are in section 241(3)(a) to (n); the last choice stands for any other interim or final order)
      `the order is made in connection with an application under section 241` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order made in connection with an application for relief from oppression?
      `the order directs the corporation to make a payment that subsection 241(6) forbids` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the order direct the corporation to make a payment that the limitation on payments to shareholders (section 241(6)) forbids?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the court make this kind of order on my oppression application` IF
    `the court may make an order of the kind within s 241(3)` `the kind of order` `the order is made in connection with an application under section 241` `the order directs the corporation to make a payment that subsection 241(6) forbids`

@export As a director, must I comply forthwith with the articles-amendment duty after an oppression order (s 241(4)(a))?
GIVEN `an order under section 241 directs amendment of the articles or by-laws` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an order made under the oppression section direct amendment of the articles or by-laws of the corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As a director, must I comply forthwith with the articles-amendment duty after an oppression order` IF
    `the directors must forthwith comply with subsection 191(4) within s 241(4)(a)` `an order under section 241 directs amendment of the articles or by-laws`

@export Is another amendment to the articles or by-laws barred, without the court's consent, after such an order (s 241(4)(b))?
GIVEN `an order under section 241 directs amendment of the articles or by-laws` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an order made under the oppression section direct amendment of the articles or by-laws of the corporation?
      `the court has consented to the other amendment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court consented to the other amendment?
      `a court has otherwise ordered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a court otherwise ordered?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is another amendment to the articles or by-laws barred, without the court's consent, after such an order` IF
    `another amendment to the articles or by-laws is barred within s 241(4)(b)` `an order under section 241 directs amendment of the articles or by-laws` `the court has consented to the other amendment` `a court has otherwise ordered`

@export Am I barred from dissenting under section 190 from an amendment to the articles made under the oppression section (s 241(5))?
GIVEN `the amendment to the articles is effected under section 241` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the amendment to the articles effected under the oppression section?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I barred from dissenting under section 190 from an amendment to the articles made under the oppression section` IF
    `a shareholder is not entitled to dissent under section 190 within s 241(5)` `the amendment to the articles is effected under section 241`

@export Must the corporation hold back a payment to me as a shareholder under an oppression order (s 241(6))?
GIVEN `the payment is to a shareholder under paragraph 241(3)(f) or (g)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment to a shareholder under an order to purchase securities or to repay money paid for securities?
      `there are reasonable grounds for believing the corporation cannot pay its liabilities as they become due` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there reasonable grounds for believing that the corporation is or would after the payment be unable to pay its liabilities as they become due?
      `there are reasonable grounds for believing the realizable value of the corporation's assets would be less than its liabilities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there reasonable grounds for believing that the realizable value of the corporation's assets would thereby be less than the total of its liabilities?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the corporation hold back a payment to me as a shareholder under an oppression order` IF
    `the corporation must not make the payment within s 241(6)` `the payment is to a shareholder under paragraph 241(3)(f) or (g)` `there are reasonable grounds for believing the corporation cannot pay its liabilities as they become due` `there are reasonable grounds for believing the realizable value of the corporation's assets would be less than its liabilities`

@export May I apply in the alternative for a dissolution order when I apply for relief from oppression (s 241(7))?
GIVEN `I am an applicant under section 241` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an applicant under the oppression section?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I apply in the alternative for a dissolution order when I apply for relief from oppression` IF
    `the applicant may apply in the alternative for an order under section 214 within s 241(7)` `I am an applicant under section 241`

-- s 242.
@export Can my application or action be stayed or dismissed only because the shareholders approved the breach (s 242(1))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my application or action be stayed or dismissed only because the shareholders approved the breach` IF
    `an application or action under Part XX is stayed or dismissed by reason only of approval by the shareholders within s 242(1)`

@export May the court take the shareholders' approval of the breach into account (s 242(1))?
GIVEN `the order is made under section 214, 240 or 241` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order made under the dissolution section (214), the derivative-action section (240) or the oppression section (241)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the court take the shareholders' approval of the breach into account` IF
    `the court may take evidence of approval by the shareholders into account within s 242(1)` `the order is made under section 214, 240 or 241`

@export Do I need the court's approval to stay, discontinue, settle or abandon my application or action (s 242(2))?
GIVEN `the step` IS A `Step in an application or action under Part XX (s 242(2))` @desc Which step is in question? (a stay, a discontinuance, a settlement, a dismissal for want of prosecution, in Quebec a dismissal for failure to respect the agreement on the conduct of the proceeding, or any other step)
      `the proceeding is in Quebec` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proceeding in Quebec?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I need the court's approval to stay, discontinue, settle or abandon my application or action` IF
    `the approval of the court is required for the step within s 242(2)` `the step` `the proceeding is in Quebec`

@export May the court order notice to me before a step is taken in an application or action (s 242(2))?
GIVEN `the court determines that my interests may be substantially affected by the step` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court determine that the interests of a complainant may be substantially affected by the step?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the court order notice to me before a step is taken in an application or action` IF
    `the court may order a party to give notice to the complainant within s 242(2)` `the court determines that my interests may be substantially affected by the step`

@export Must I give security for costs in my application or action under the remedies Part (s 242(3))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I give security for costs in my application or action under the remedies Part` IF
    `a complainant is required to give security for costs within s 242(3)`

@export May the court order the corporation to pay my interim costs (s 242(4))?
GIVEN `my application or action is made, brought or intervened in under the remedies Part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your application or action made, brought or intervened in under the remedies Part?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the court order the corporation to pay my interim costs` IF
    `the court may order the corporation or its subsidiary to pay interim costs to the complainant within s 242(4)` `my application or action is made, brought or intervened in under the remedies Part`

@export Can I be held accountable for the interim costs when my case ends (s 242(4))?
GIVEN `interim costs were ordered to be paid to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were interim costs ordered to be paid to you?
      `my application or action has reached its final disposition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your application or action reached its final disposition?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be held accountable for the interim costs when my case ends` IF
    `the complainant may be held accountable for the interim costs within s 242(4)` `interim costs were ordered to be paid to me` `my application or action has reached its final disposition`

-- s 243.
@export May I apply to the court to rectify the registers or records of the corporation (s 243(1))?
GIVEN `I am the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the corporation itself?
      `I am a security holder of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a security holder of the corporation?
      `I am an aggrieved person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an aggrieved person?
      `a name is alleged to be wrongly entered, retained, deleted or omitted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the name of a person alleged to be, or to have been, wrongly entered or retained in, or wrongly deleted or omitted from, the registers or other records of the corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I apply to the court to rectify the registers or records of the corporation` IF
    `may apply to a court for an order that the registers or records be rectified within s 243(1)` applicant `a name is alleged to be wrongly entered, retained, deleted or omitted` `I am an aggrieved person`
    WHERE
        applicant MEANS IF `I am the corporation` THEN `the corporation`
                        ELSE IF `I am a security holder of the corporation` THEN `a security holder`
                              ELSE `any person`

@export Must I give the Director notice of my application to rectify the registers (s 243(2))?
GIVEN `I am an applicant under section 243` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an applicant under the rectification section?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I give the Director notice of my application to rectify the registers` IF
    `the applicant must give the Director notice within s 243(2)` `I am an applicant under section 243`

@export Is the Director entitled to appear and be heard on my application to rectify the registers (s 243(2))?
GIVEN `an application has been made under section 243` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an application been made to the court to rectify the registers or records?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the Director entitled to appear and be heard on my application to rectify the registers` IF
    `the Director is entitled to appear and be heard within s 243(2)` `an application has been made under section 243`

@export May the court make this kind of order on an application to rectify the registers (s 243(3))?
GIVEN `the kind of order` IS A `Kind of order on an application to rectify records (s 243(3))` @desc Which kind of order is in question? (the listed kinds are in section 243(3)(a) to (d); the last choice stands for any other order)
      `the order is made in connection with an application under section 243` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order made in connection with an application to rectify the registers or records?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the court make this kind of order on an application to rectify the registers` IF
    `the court may make an order of the kind within s 243(3)` `the kind of order` `the order is made in connection with an application under section 243`

-- s 245. What the Director owes me when I file articles or a document, and what follows.
@export By what day must the Director give me written notice that it has refused to file my document (s 245(1))?
GIVEN `the day the Director received my articles or document` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the Director receive your articles or other document?
      `an approval is required under another Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an approval required under another Act before the document can be filed?
      `the day the Director received that approval` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the Director receive that approval? (any date if none is required)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must the Director give me written notice that it has refused to file my document` IS
    `the last day for the Director to give written notice of the refusal within s 245(1)` `the day the Director received my articles or document` approval
    WHERE
        approval MEANS IF `an approval is required under another Act` THEN JUST `the day the Director received that approval` ELSE NOTHING

@export Has the Director given me written notice of the refusal in time (s 245(1))?
GIVEN `the Director refused to file my document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Director refused to file the articles or other document that the Act requires the Director to file before it becomes effective?
      `the Director has given me written notice of the refusal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Director given you written notice of the refusal, with reasons?
      `the day the Director gave notice` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the Director give the notice? (any date if not given)
      `the last day for the Director to give written notice of the refusal` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for the Director to give written notice of the refusal? (twenty days after the Director received the document, or after any approval required under another Act, whichever is later)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the Director given me written notice of the refusal in time` IF
    `the Director has complied with the duty to give notice of the refusal within s 245(1)` `the Director refused to file my document` notified `the last day for the Director to give written notice of the refusal`
    WHERE
        notified MEANS IF `the Director has given me written notice of the refusal` THEN JUST `the day the Director gave notice` ELSE NOTHING

@export Is the Director deemed to have refused to file my document (s 245(2))?
GIVEN `the day it is asked` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking?
      `the last day for the Director to give written notice of the refusal` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for the Director to give written notice of a refusal? (twenty days after the Director received the document, or after any approval required under another Act, whichever is later)
      `the Director has filed the document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Director filed your document?
      `the day the Director filed the document` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the Director file it? (any date if not filed)
      `the Director has given written notice of the refusal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Director given you written notice of the refusal to file?
      `the day the Director gave notice of the refusal` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the Director give the notice? (any date if not given)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the Director deemed to have refused to file my document` IF
    `the Director is deemed to have refused to file the document for the purposes of s 246 within s 245(2)` `the day it is asked` `the last day for the Director to give written notice of the refusal` filed notified
    WHERE
        filed MEANS IF `the Director has filed the document` THEN JUST `the day the Director filed the document` ELSE NOTHING
        notified MEANS IF `the Director has given written notice of the refusal` THEN JUST `the day the Director gave notice of the refusal` ELSE NOTHING

-- s 246. Appeal from the Director's decision.
@export May I apply to the court about this decision of the Director (s 246)?
GIVEN `the kind of decision` IS A `Kind of decision of the Director that may be appealed (s 246)` @desc Which kind of decision is it? (the listed kinds are in section 246(a) to (g); the last choice stands for any other decision of the Director)
      `I feel aggrieved by the decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you feel aggrieved by the decision?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I apply to the court about this decision of the Director` IF
    `a person may apply to a court for an order on the decision within s 246` `the kind of decision` `I feel aggrieved by the decision`

@export May the court make any order it thinks fit on my appeal from the Director's decision (s 246)?
GIVEN `an application has been made under section 246` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an application been made to the court under the appeal section?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the court make any order it thinks fit on my appeal from the Director's decision` IF
    `the court may make any order it thinks fit on the appeal within s 246` `an application has been made under section 246`

-- s 247. The claim of a complainant or creditor, and the exposure of a director, officer or the corporation.
@export May I apply to the court for an order that the corporation or one of its people comply with the Act (s 247)?
GIVEN `I am a complainant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a complainant (a current or former security holder, a current or former director or officer, the Director, or a person the court finds proper)?
      `I am a creditor of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a creditor of the corporation?
      `the respondent is the corporation or one of the persons the section names` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the respondent the corporation, or a director, officer, employee, agent or mandatary, auditor, trustee, receiver, receiver-manager, sequestrator or liquidator of it?
      `the respondent does not comply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the respondent not comply with the Act, the regulations, the articles or by-laws, or a unanimous shareholder agreement?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I apply to the court for an order that the corporation or one of its people comply with the Act` IF
    `may apply to a court for a compliance or restraining order within s 247` `I am a complainant` `I am a creditor of the corporation` `the respondent is the corporation or one of the persons the section names` `the respondent does not comply`

@export As a director or officer, can a complainant or creditor ask the court to order me to comply (s 247)?
GIVEN `the applicant is a complainant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person asking a complainant?
      `the applicant is a creditor of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person asking a creditor of the corporation?
      `I do not comply with the Act, the regulations, the articles or by-laws, or a unanimous shareholder agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you fail to comply with the Act, the regulations, the articles or by-laws, or a unanimous shareholder agreement?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As a director or officer, can a complainant or creditor ask the court to order me to comply` IF
    `may apply to a court for a compliance or restraining order within s 247` `the applicant is a complainant` `the applicant is a creditor of the corporation` TRUE `I do not comply with the Act, the regulations, the articles or by-laws, or a unanimous shareholder agreement`

@export May my application be made in a summary manner (s 248)?
GIVEN `the Act states that a person may apply to a court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Act state that a person may apply to a court for what you want?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my application be made in a summary manner` IF
    `the application may be made in a summary manner within s 248` `the Act states that a person may apply to a court`

@export Can I appeal an order made under the Act, and do I need leave (s 249)?
GIVEN `the order was made by a court of a province under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the order made by a court of a province under the Act?
      `the order is a final order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a final order?
GIVETH A `Whether an appeal lies (s 249)`
DECIDE `Can I appeal an order made under the Act, and do I need leave` IS
    `whether an appeal lies within s 249` `the order was made by a court of a province under the Act` `the order is a final order`

§§ `Offences and punishment (Part XX)`

-- s 250. A false or misleading report, return, notice or document; the register of individuals with significant
-- control is not one; and the immunity of someone who did not know and could not have known.
@export Am I guilty of an offence for a false or misleading report, return, notice or document (s 250(1), (3), (4))?
GIVEN `I made or helped make the document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make, or assist in making, the report, return, notice or other document?
      `the document is required by the Act or the regulations to be sent to the Director or another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document one that the Act or the regulations require to be sent to the Director or to any other person?
      `it is a register of individuals with significant control or an extract from it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document the register of individuals with significant control, or an extract from it?
      `it contains an untrue statement of a material fact` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it contain an untrue statement of a material fact?
      `it omits to state a material fact required in it or needed so that a statement is not misleading` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it omit to state a material fact required in it, or necessary to make a statement in it not misleading in the circumstances in which it was made?
      `I did not know of the untrue statement or omission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you not know of the untrue statement or omission?
      `with reasonable diligence I could not have known` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the exercise of reasonable diligence, could you not have known of it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I guilty of an offence for a false or misleading report, return, notice or document` IF
    `the person is guilty of an offence within s 250(1) and s 250(3)` elements immunity
    WHERE
        elements MEANS `the elements of the offence are met within s 250(1)` `I made or helped make the document` `the document is required by the Act or the regulations to be sent to the Director or another person` isReport `it contains an untrue statement of a material fact` `it omits to state a material fact required in it or needed so that a statement is not misleading`
        isReport MEANS `the document is a report, return, notice or other document for the purposes of s 250 within s 250(4)` TRUE `it is a register of individuals with significant control or an extract from it`
        immunity MEANS `the person has the immunity within s 250(3)` `I did not know of the untrue statement or omission` `with reasonable diligence I could not have known`

@export What is the largest fine I could face for a false or misleading document (dollars) (s 250(1))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the largest fine I could face for a false or misleading document` IS
    (`the most the court may impose within s 250(1)`)'s `largest fine in dollars`

@export What is the longest imprisonment I could face for a false or misleading document (months) (s 250(1))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the longest imprisonment I could face for a false or misleading document` IS
    (`the most the court may impose within s 250(1)`)'s `longest imprisonment in months`

@export As a director or officer, am I guilty when my body corporate files a false or misleading document (s 250(2))?
GIVEN `the body corporate commits an offence under subsection 250(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the body corporate committed the offence of a false or misleading report, return, notice or document?
      `I am a director or officer of the body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director or officer of the body corporate?
      `I knowingly authorized, permitted or acquiesced in the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you knowingly authorize, permit or acquiesce in the commission of the offence?
      `I did not know of the untrue statement or omission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you not know of the untrue statement or omission?
      `with reasonable diligence I could not have known` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the exercise of reasonable diligence, could you not have known of it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As a director or officer, am I guilty when my body corporate files a false or misleading document` IF
    `the director or officer is a party to and guilty of the offence within s 250(2)` `the body corporate commits an offence under subsection 250(1)` `I am a director or officer of the body corporate` `I knowingly authorized, permitted or acquiesced in the offence` immunity
    WHERE
        immunity MEANS `the person has the immunity within s 250(3)` `I did not know of the untrue statement or omission` `with reasonable diligence I could not have known`

@export What is the largest fine I could face as a director or officer who authorized the false or misleading document (dollars) (s 250(2))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the largest fine I could face as a director or officer who authorized the false or misleading document` IS
    (`the most the court may impose on a director or officer within s 250(2)`)'s `largest fine in dollars`

@export What is the longest imprisonment I could face as a director or officer who authorized the false or misleading document (months) (s 250(2))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the longest imprisonment I could face as a director or officer who authorized the false or misleading document` IS
    (`the most the court may impose on a director or officer within s 250(2)`)'s `longest imprisonment in months`

-- s 251. The general offence: no punishment is provided, no reasonable cause.
@export Am I guilty of an offence for contravening a provision that has no stated punishment (s 251)?
GIVEN `I contravened a provision of the Act or the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you contravene a provision of the Act or the regulations?
      `no punishment is provided for the provision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is no punishment provided for that provision?
      `I had reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have reasonable cause?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I guilty of an offence for contravening a provision that has no stated punishment` IF
    `the person is guilty of an offence within s 251` `I contravened a provision of the Act or the regulations` `no punishment is provided for the provision` `I had reasonable cause`

@export Does the Act itself state a maximum punishment for the general offence (s 251)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Act itself state a maximum punishment for the general offence` IF
    CONSIDER `the most the court may impose within s 251`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST p THEN TRUE

-- s 252. Order to comply, the limitation period, and civil remedies.
@export Can the court order me to comply with the Act after I am convicted (s 252(1))?
GIVEN `I am guilty of an offence under the Act or the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you guilty of an offence under the Act or the regulations?
      `I have been convicted of the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been convicted of the contravention?
      `proceedings for the offence are taken in the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are proceedings in respect of the offence taken in the court?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the court order me to comply with the Act after I am convicted` IF
    `the court may order the person to comply within s 252(1)` `I am guilty of an offence under the Act or the regulations` `I have been convicted of the contravention` `proceedings for the offence are taken in the court`

@export By what day can a prosecution be brought against me for an offence under the Act (s 252(2))?
GIVEN `the day the subject-matter of the complaint arose` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the subject-matter of the complaint arise?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day can a prosecution be brought against me for an offence under the Act` IS
    `the last day to institute a prosecution within s 252(2)` `the day the subject-matter of the complaint arose`

@export Is it too late to prosecute me for an offence under the Act (s 252(2))?
GIVEN `the day the subject-matter of the complaint arose` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the subject-matter of the complaint arise?
      `the day the prosecution is instituted` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the prosecution instituted?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it too late to prosecute me for an offence under the Act` IF
    NOT `the prosecution is instituted in time within s 252(2)` `the day the subject-matter of the complaint arose` `the day the prosecution is instituted`

@export Is my civil remedy suspended or affected because the same act is an offence under the Act (s 252(3))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my civil remedy suspended or affected because the same act is an offence under the Act` IF
    `a civil remedy is suspended or affected by reason that the act or omission is an offence under this Act within s 252(3)`

§§ `Electronic documents (Part XX.1)`

-- s 252.1. The Part's own words: "electronic document" and "information system".
@export Is this an electronic document within the electronic-document rules (s 252.1)?
GIVEN `it is a form of representation of information or of concepts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a form of representation of information or of concepts?
      `it is fixed in a medium in or by electronic, optical or other similar means` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it fixed in a medium in or by electronic, optical or other similar means?
      `it can be read or perceived by a person or by any means` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can it be read or perceived by a person or by any means?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this an electronic document within the electronic-document rules` IF
    `electronic document within s 252.1` `it is a form of representation of information or of concepts` `it is fixed in a medium in or by electronic, optical or other similar means` `it can be read or perceived by a person or by any means`

@export Is this an information system within the electronic-document rules (s 252.1)?
GIVEN `it is a system used to generate, send, receive, store or otherwise process an electronic document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a system used to generate, send, receive, store or otherwise process an electronic document?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this an information system within the electronic-document rules` IF
    `information system within s 252.1` `it is a system used to generate, send, receive, store or otherwise process an electronic document`

-- s 252.2. The Part reaches everything except what is sent to or issued by the Director and what the
-- regulations carve out.
@export Do the electronic-document rules cover this notice or document (s 252.2)?
GIVEN `the notice, document or other information is sent to or issued by the Director pursuant to this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice, document or other information sent to, or issued by, the Director under the Act?
      `the notice, document or other information is prescribed to be outside the Part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the regulations say that this notice, document or information is outside the electronic-documents rules?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the electronic-document rules cover this notice or document` IF
    `Part XX.1 applies within s 252.2` `the notice, document or other information is sent to or issued by the Director pursuant to this Act` `the notice, document or other information is prescribed to be outside the Part`

-- s 252.3(1). Nobody can be made to use electronic documents.
@export Can the Act or the regulations force me to create or provide an electronic document (s 252.3(1))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Act or the regulations force me to create or provide an electronic document` IF
    `this Act or the regulations require a person to create or provide an electronic document within s 252.3(1)`

-- s 252.3(2), (3). The addressee's claim, and the corresponding position of whoever must provide the notice.
@export Does an electronic document count as my having been given a notice (s 252.3(2))?
GIVEN `I consented in the manner prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you consented, in the manner prescribed, to receiving electronic documents?
      `I revoked my consent in the manner prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you revoked that consent in the manner prescribed?
      `I designated an information system for the receipt of the electronic document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you designated an information system for the receipt of the electronic document?
      `it was provided to the information system I designated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the electronic document provided to the information system you designated?
      `the regulations say how else it is to be provided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the regulations otherwise prescribe how the electronic document is to be provided?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does an electronic document count as my having been given a notice` IF
    `the provision of an electronic document satisfies the requirement to provide it to the addressee within s 252.3(2)` `I consented in the manner prescribed` `I revoked my consent in the manner prescribed` `I designated an information system for the receipt of the electronic document` `it was provided to the information system I designated` `the regulations say how else it is to be provided`

@export As the corporation, have I satisfied my duty to give a shareholder a notice by sending an electronic document (s 252.3(2), s 252.4)?
GIVEN `the addressee consented in the manner prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person to be given the notice consented, in the manner prescribed, to receiving electronic documents?
      `the addressee revoked the consent in the manner prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the addressee revoked that consent in the manner prescribed?
      `the addressee designated an information system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the addressee designated an information system for the receipt of the electronic document?
      `I provided it to the designated information system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you provide the electronic document to the designated information system?
      `the regulations say how else it is to be provided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the regulations otherwise prescribe how the electronic document is to be provided?
      `the articles or by-laws provide otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the articles or by-laws of the corporation provide otherwise than that an electronic document may be used?
      `the regulations, if any, have been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the regulations, if any, been complied with?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the corporation, have I satisfied my duty to give a shareholder a notice by sending an electronic document` IF
    `an electronic document satisfies a requirement to provide a notice to a person within s 252.3(2) and s 252.4` creation provision
    WHERE
        creation MEANS `an electronic document satisfies the requirement to create or provide within s 252.4` `the articles or by-laws provide otherwise` `the regulations, if any, have been complied with`
        provision MEANS `the provision of an electronic document satisfies the requirement to provide it to the addressee within s 252.3(2)` `the addressee consented in the manner prescribed` `the addressee revoked the consent in the manner prescribed` `the addressee designated an information system` `I provided it to the designated information system` `the regulations say how else it is to be provided`

@export Does my withdrawal of consent to electronic documents take effect (s 252.3(3))?
GIVEN `I consented under paragraph 252.3(2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you consented to receiving electronic documents?
      `I revoke the consent in the manner prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you revoking the consent in the manner prescribed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my withdrawal of consent to electronic documents take effect` IF
    `the revocation takes effect within s 252.3(3)` `I consented under paragraph 252.3(2)(a)` `I revoke the consent in the manner prescribed`

-- s 252.4, 252.5.
@export Can I use an electronic document to create or provide a document the Act requires (s 252.4)?
GIVEN `the by-laws or the articles of the corporation provide otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the by-laws or the articles of the corporation provide otherwise than that an electronic document may be used?
      `the regulations, if any, have been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the regulations, if any, been complied with?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I use an electronic document to create or provide a document the Act requires` IF
    `an electronic document satisfies the requirement to create or provide within s 252.4` `the by-laws or the articles of the corporation provide otherwise` `the regulations, if any, have been complied with`

@export Does an electronic document satisfy a requirement that I create a document in writing (s 252.5(1))?
GIVEN `the conditions in section 252.4 are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the conditions for using an electronic document (the articles and by-laws do not provide otherwise, and the regulations are complied with) met?
      `the information is accessible so as to be usable for subsequent reference` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information in the electronic document accessible so as to be usable for subsequent reference?
      `the regulations pertaining to subsection 252.5(1), if any, have been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the regulations pertaining to this subsection, if any, been complied with?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does an electronic document satisfy a requirement that I create a document in writing` IF
    `an electronic document satisfies the requirement to create in writing within s 252.5(1)` `the conditions in section 252.4 are met` `the information is accessible so as to be usable for subsequent reference` `the regulations pertaining to subsection 252.5(1), if any, have been complied with`

@export Does an electronic document satisfy a requirement that I be provided with a document in writing (s 252.5(2))?
GIVEN `the conditions in section 252.4 are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the conditions for using an electronic document (the articles and by-laws do not provide otherwise, and the regulations are complied with) met?
      `the information is accessible by me and I can retain it so as to be usable for subsequent reference` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information accessible by you and capable of being retained by you, so as to be usable for subsequent reference?
      `the regulations pertaining to subsection 252.5(2), if any, have been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the regulations pertaining to this subsection, if any, been complied with?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does an electronic document satisfy a requirement that I be provided with a document in writing` IF
    `an electronic document satisfies the requirement to provide in writing within s 252.5(2)` `the conditions in section 252.4 are met` `the information is accessible by me and I can retain it so as to be usable for subsequent reference` `the regulations pertaining to subsection 252.5(2), if any, have been complied with`

@export Does one electronic version satisfy a requirement to give me several copies at once (s 252.5(3))?
GIVEN `the requirement is for copies to be provided to a single addressee at the same time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the requirement that one or more copies of a document be provided to a single addressee at the same time?
      `a single version of the electronic document is provided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a single version of the electronic document provided?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does one electronic version satisfy a requirement to give me several copies at once` IF
    `a single version of an electronic document satisfies the requirement for copies within s 252.5(3)` `the requirement is for copies to be provided to a single addressee at the same time` `a single version of the electronic document is provided`

@export Does sending an electronic document satisfy a requirement to send something by registered mail (s 252.5(4))?
GIVEN `the requirement is to provide a document by registered mail` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the requirement to provide a document by registered mail?
      `the regulations prescribe that sending an electronic document satisfies it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the regulations prescribe that sending an electronic document satisfies that requirement?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does sending an electronic document satisfy a requirement to send something by registered mail` IF
    `sending an electronic document satisfies the requirement to provide by registered mail within s 252.5(4)` `the requirement is to provide a document by registered mail` `the regulations prescribe that sending an electronic document satisfies it`

-- s 252.6, 252.7.
@export May I make my statutory declaration or affidavit as an electronic document (s 252.6(1))?
GIVEN `I sign it with my secure electronic signature` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you sign it with your secure electronic signature (as defined in the federal electronic documents Act)?
      `the person before whom it is made signs it with their secure electronic signature` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the authorized person before whom it is made sign it with their secure electronic signature?
      `the requirements for electronic documents in sections 252.3 to 252.5 are complied with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the requirements for electronic documents in sections 252.3 to 252.5 complied with?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I make my statutory declaration or affidavit as an electronic document` IF
    `a statutory declaration or affidavit may be created or provided in an electronic document within s 252.6(1)` `I sign it with my secure electronic signature` `the person before whom it is made signs it with their secure electronic signature` `the requirements for electronic documents in sections 252.3 to 252.5 are complied with`

@export Is this an electronic document for the purposes of a statutory declaration or affidavit (s 252.6(2))?
GIVEN `it is an electronic document within the meaning of subsection 31(1) of the federal electronic documents Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an electronic document within the meaning of subsection 31(1) of the Personal Information Protection and Electronic Documents Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this an electronic document for the purposes of a statutory declaration or affidavit` IF
    `electronic document within s 252.6` `it is an electronic document within the meaning of subsection 31(1) of the federal electronic documents Act`

@export Does an electronic signature satisfy the Act's requirement for my signature (s 252.7)?
GIVEN `the document is a statutory declaration or an affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document a statutory declaration or an affidavit?
      `the prescribed requirements, if any, are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the requirements prescribed for this section, if any, met?
      `the signature is unique to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can it be proven that the signature resulting from the technology or process is unique to you?
      `the technology attaches my signature to the document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can it be proven that the technology or process is used to incorporate, attach or associate your signature to the electronic document?
      `the technology can identify me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can it be proven that the technology or process can be used to identify you?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does an electronic signature satisfy the Act's requirement for my signature` IF
    `a requirement for a signature or for a document to be executed is satisfied within s 252.7` `the document is a statutory declaration or an affidavit` `the prescribed requirements, if any, are met` `the signature is unique to me` `the technology attaches my signature to the document` `the technology can identify me`

§§ `Notices to and from the corporation (Part XXI)`

-- s 253(1). The corporation's way of sending: prepaid mail or personal delivery, to the latest address of
-- record; the claim is the shareholder's or director's.
@export Has the corporation sent me a notice in a way the Act allows (s 253(1))?
GIVEN `I am a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of the corporation? (answer no if you are a shareholder)
      way IS A `Way of sending a notice (s 253(1))` @desc How was the notice sent? (by prepaid mail, by personal delivery, or in some other way)
      `it was addressed to my latest address in the corporation's or its transfer agent's records` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are a shareholder: was it addressed to your latest address as shown in the records of the corporation or its transfer agent?
      `it was addressed to my latest address in the corporation's records or the last notice filed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are a director: was it addressed to your latest address as shown in the records of the corporation or in the last notice filed with the Director?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the corporation sent me a notice in a way the Act allows` IF
    `a notice or document may be sent in the way within s 253(1)` recipient way `it was addressed to my latest address in the corporation's or its transfer agent's records` `it was addressed to my latest address in the corporation's records or the last notice filed`
    WHERE
        recipient MEANS IF `I am a director` THEN `a director` ELSE `a shareholder`

@export Am I presumed to be a director of the corporation because I am named in a filed notice (s 253(2))?
GIVEN `I am named as a director in a notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you named as a director in a notice?
      `the notice was sent by a corporation to the Director under section 106 or 113` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice sent by a corporation to the Director as a notice of directors or of change of directors?
      `the notice was filed by the Director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it filed by the Director?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I presumed to be a director of the corporation because I am named in a filed notice` IF
    `the person is presumed to be a director of the corporation within s 253(2)` `I am named as a director in a notice` `the notice was sent by a corporation to the Director under section 106 or 113` `the notice was filed by the Director`

-- s 253(3). When the notice counts as received; the rule gives a date or none.
@export On what day am I treated as having received a notice mailed to me (s 253(3))?
GIVEN `I am a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of the corporation? (answer no if you are a shareholder)
      `the notice was sent in accordance with subsection 253(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice sent in the way the Act allows (prepaid mail or personal delivery to your latest address of record)?
      `I did not receive it at that time or at all, and there are reasonable grounds for believing so` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there reasonable grounds for believing that you did not receive the notice at the time it would be delivered in the ordinary course of mail, or at all?
      `the day it would be delivered in the ordinary course of mail` IS A DATE @desc On what day would it be delivered in the ordinary course of mail?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On what day am I treated as having received a notice mailed to me` IS
    `the date the notice is deemed received within s 253(3)` `the notice was sent in accordance with subsection 253(1)` recipient `I did not receive it at that time or at all, and there are reasonable grounds for believing so` `the day it would be delivered in the ordinary course of mail`
    WHERE
        recipient MEANS IF `I am a director` THEN `a director` ELSE `a shareholder`

@export Can the corporation stop sending me notices because they keep coming back (s 253(4))?
GIVEN `the number of consecutive notices returned because I cannot be found` IS A NUMBER @desc How many notices sent to you in the Act's way have been returned, on consecutive occasions, because you cannot be found?
      `I have told the corporation my new address in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you informed the corporation in writing of your new address?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the corporation stop sending me notices because they keep coming back` IF
    `the corporation is not required to send further notices to the shareholder within s 253(4)` `the number of consecutive notices returned because I cannot be found` `I have told the corporation my new address in writing`

-- s 254. Notices to the corporation.
@export May I send a notice or document to the corporation, or serve it, by registered mail (s 254)?
GIVEN `I send it by registered mail` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you send it by registered mail?
      `it is addressed to the corporation's registered office in the last notice filed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it addressed to the registered office of the corporation shown in the last notice filed with the Director?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I send a notice or document to the corporation, or serve it, by registered mail` IF
    `a notice or document may be sent to or served on a corporation within s 254` `I send it by registered mail` `it is addressed to the corporation's registered office in the last notice filed`

@export On what day is my notice to the corporation treated as received or served (s 254)?
GIVEN `my notice or document was sent as section 254 allows` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your notice or document sent to the corporation in the way section 254 allows?
      `there are reasonable grounds for believing the corporation did not receive it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there reasonable grounds for believing that the corporation did not receive the notice or document at that time or at all?
      `the day it would be delivered in the ordinary course of mail` IS A DATE @desc On what day would it be delivered in the ordinary course of mail?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On what day is my notice to the corporation treated as received or served` IS
    `the date the notice is deemed received or served within s 254` `my notice or document was sent as section 254 allows` `there are reasonable grounds for believing the corporation did not receive it` `the day it would be delivered in the ordinary course of mail`

-- s 255.
@export Can the sending of a notice to me, or its time, be waived (s 255)?
GIVEN `the notice or document is required by the Act or the regulations to be sent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice or document one the Act or the regulations require to be sent?
      `I am entitled to it and have consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to the notice or document, and have you consented in writing to waive or abridge its sending or time?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the sending of a notice to me, or its time, be waived` IF
    `the sending or the time may be waived or abridged within s 255` `the notice or document is required by the Act or the regulations to be sent` `I am entitled to it and have consented in writing`

-- s 256. Certificates of the Director, and their weight in proof.
@export Is a certificate of the Director signed validly (s 256(1))?
GIVEN `it is signed by the Director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the certificate signed by the Director?
      `it is signed by a Deputy Director authorized under section 260` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it signed by a Deputy Director authorized under the section on delegation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a certificate of the Director signed validly` IF
    `the certificate of the Director is validly signed within s 256(1)` `it is signed by the Director` `it is signed by a Deputy Director authorized under section 260`

@export How much proof is a certificate of the Director (s 256(2))?
GIVEN `it is a certificate referred to in subsection 256(1) or a certified copy of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a certificate of the Director referred to in the validly-signed section, or a certified copy of one?
      `it is introduced as evidence in a civil, criminal or administrative action or proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it introduced as evidence in a civil, criminal or administrative action or proceeding?
      `the proceeding is a proceeding under section 213 to dissolve a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proceeding one under the dissolution section (section 213)?
GIVETH A `Strength of proof given by the Act (ss 256(2), 257(2))`
DECIDE `How much proof is a certificate of the Director` IS
    `the strength of proof of a certificate of the Director within s 256(2)` `it is a certificate referred to in subsection 256(1) or a certified copy of it` `it is introduced as evidence in a civil, criminal or administrative action or proceeding` `the proceeding is a proceeding under section 213 to dissolve a corporation`

-- s 257. Certificates of a corporation, and what the register proves.
@export May a certificate issued for the corporation be signed by me (s 257(1))?
GIVEN `the certificate states a fact set out in the articles, the by-laws, a unanimous shareholder agreement, the minutes or a contract of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate state a fact that is set out in the articles, the by-laws, a unanimous shareholder agreement, the minutes of meetings of the directors, a committee of directors or the shareholders, or a trust indenture or other contract to which the corporation is a party?
      `I am a director of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of the corporation?
      `I am an officer of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the corporation?
      `I am a transfer agent of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a transfer agent of the corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a certificate issued for the corporation be signed by me` IF
    `a certificate issued on behalf of a corporation may be signed by the person within s 257(1)` `the certificate states a fact set out in the articles, the by-laws, a unanimous shareholder agreement, the minutes or a contract of the corporation` `I am a director of the corporation` `I am an officer of the corporation` `I am a transfer agent of the corporation`

@export How much proof is a certificate, extract or minutes of the corporation (s 257(2))?
GIVEN `it is a fact stated in a certificate referred to in subsection 257(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a fact stated in a corporation's certificate signed by a director, officer or transfer agent?
      `it is a certified extract from a securities register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a certified extract from a securities register of a corporation?
      `it is a certified copy of minutes or an extract from minutes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a certified copy of minutes, or an extract from minutes, of a meeting of shareholders, directors or a committee of directors?
      `it is introduced as evidence in a civil, criminal or administrative action or proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it introduced as evidence in a civil, criminal or administrative action or proceeding?
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there evidence to the contrary?
GIVETH A `Strength of proof given by the Act (ss 256(2), 257(2))`
DECIDE `How much proof is a certificate, extract or minutes of the corporation` IS
    `the strength of proof of a corporation's certificate, extract or minutes within s 257(2)` `it is a fact stated in a certificate referred to in subsection 257(1)` `it is a certified extract from a securities register` `it is a certified copy of minutes or an extract from minutes` `it is introduced as evidence in a civil, criminal or administrative action or proceeding` `there is evidence to the contrary`

@export Does the securities register show that I own my shares (s 257(3))?
GIVEN `it is an entry in the securities register or a security certificate issued by the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an entry in a securities register of the corporation, or a security certificate issued by it?
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there evidence to the contrary?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the securities register show that I own my shares` IF
    `the entry or certificate is proof that the registered person is the owner of the securities within s 257(3)` `it is an entry in the securities register or a security certificate issued by the corporation` `there is evidence to the contrary`

§§ `Dealing with the Director (Part XXI)`

-- s 258, 258.2. What I may send, and when I may be excused from sending.
@export May I send the Director a photocopy of a document the Act requires (s 258)?
GIVEN `a notice or document is required to be sent to the Director under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice or document one that the Act requires to be sent to the Director?
      `the document I send is a photostatic or photographic copy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document you send a photostatic or photographic copy?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I send the Director a photocopy of a document the Act requires` IF
    `the Director may accept a photostatic or photographic copy within s 258` `a notice or document is required to be sent to the Director under the Act` `the document I send is a photostatic or photographic copy`

@export Can the Director excuse me from sending certain notices or documents (s 258.2)?
GIVEN `the circumstances are those prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the circumstances those prescribed by the regulations?
      `the notices contain information similar to what another Act requires to be made public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the notices or documents contain information similar to that in notices or documents required to be made public under another Act of Parliament or of a provincial legislature, as the Director specifies?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Director excuse me from sending certain notices or documents` IF
    `the Director may exempt the notices or documents from being sent to the Director within s 258.2` `the circumstances are those prescribed` `the notices contain information similar to what another Act requires to be made public`

-- s 259. The Director's power over me (verification) and the ways I may verify.
@export Can the Director require me to prove a document I sent (s 259(1))?
GIVEN `the Act or the regulations require the document, or the fact stated in it, to be sent to the Director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document, or a fact stated in the document or in other information, one that the Act or the regulations require to be sent to the Director?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Director require me to prove a document I sent` IF
    `the Director may require verification within s 259(1)` `the Act or the regulations require the document, or the fact stated in it, to be sent to the Director`

@export Is my document properly verified (s 259(2))?
GIVEN `I verified it by affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it verified by affidavit?
      `I verified it by statutory declaration under the Canada Evidence Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it verified by statutory declaration under the Canada Evidence Act?
      `it is made before a commissioner for oaths or for taking affidavits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made before a commissioner for oaths or for taking affidavits?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my document properly verified` IF
    `the document or fact is verified within s 259(2)` `I verified it by affidavit` `I verified it by statutory declaration under the Canada Evidence Act` `it is made before a commissioner for oaths or for taking affidavits`

-- s 261.1.
@export When must I pay the Director's fee (s 261.1)?
GIVEN `the step` IS A `Step for which a fee is payable (s 261.1)` @desc Which step is the fee payable for? (receipt or copying of a document or other information; or the examination, filing or issuance of one, or an action the Director must or may take)
GIVETH A `When a fee must be paid (s 261.1)`
DECIDE `When must I pay the Director's fee` IS
    `when the fee must be paid to the Director within s 261.1` `the step`

-- s 262. What I am owed once I send articles or a statement: the four duties of the Director are my four claims.
@export Is the Director now bound to do this on my articles or statement (s 262(2))?
GIVEN `the duty` IS A `Duty of the Director on receiving articles or a statement (s 262(2))` @desc Which duty is in question? (to record the date of receipt; to issue the appropriate certificate; to send the certificate to the corporation or its agent; or to publish a notice of the issuance of the certificate)
      `the Act requires the articles or statement to be sent to the Director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Act require the articles or statement relating to the corporation to be sent to the Director?
      `the Director has received them in the form the Director fixes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Director received them in the form the Director fixes?
      `the Director has received any other required documents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Director received any other required documents?
      `the Director has received the required fees` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Director received the required fees?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the Director now bound to do this on my articles or statement` IF
    `the duty is due within s 262(2)` `the duty` `the Act requires the articles or statement to be sent to the Director` `the Director has received them in the form the Director fixes` `the Director has received any other required documents` `the Director has received the required fees`

@export Is a statement of intent to dissolve, or of its revocation, a statement for the Director's certificate (s 262(1))?
GIVEN `it is a statement of intent to dissolve referred to in section 211` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a statement of intent to dissolve referred to in section 211?
      `it is a statement of revocation of intent to dissolve referred to in section 211` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a statement of revocation of intent to dissolve referred to in section 211?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a statement of intent to dissolve, or of its revocation, a statement for the Director's certificate` IF
    `statement within s 262(1)` `it is a statement of intent to dissolve referred to in section 211` `it is a statement of revocation of intent to dissolve referred to in section 211`

@export Can the Director's certificate be dated as of the day I name (s 262(3))?
GIVEN `the day the certificate is to be dated as of` IS A DATE @desc As of what day do you want the certificate to be dated?
      `the day the Director receives the articles, statement or court order` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the Director receive the articles, statement or court order?
      `the day was specified by the court or by the person who signed the articles or statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that day specified by the court or by the person who signed the articles or statement?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Director's certificate be dated as of the day I name` IF
    `a certificate may be dated as of the day within s 262(3)` `the day the certificate is to be dated as of` `the day the Director receives the articles, statement or court order` `the day was specified by the court or by the person who signed the articles or statement`

@export Can a certificate of discontinuance be dated as of the day I name (s 262(5))?
GIVEN `it is a certificate of discontinuance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a certificate of discontinuance?
      `the day is the day the corporation amalgamates under another Act or is continued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the day you name the day on which the corporation amalgamates under another Act or is continued?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a certificate of discontinuance be dated as of the day I name` IF
    `a certificate of discontinuance may be dated as of the day within s 262(5)` `it is a certificate of discontinuance` `the day is the day the corporation amalgamates under another Act or is continued`

@export Is a mechanically reproduced signature on the Director's certificate allowed (s 262.1(1))?
GIVEN `the signature is printed or otherwise mechanically reproduced on the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the signature printed or otherwise mechanically reproduced on the certificate?
      `the signature is in accordance with the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the signature in accordance with the regulations made about signatures on certificates?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a mechanically reproduced signature on the Director's certificate allowed` IF
    `a signature on a certificate issued by the Director is allowed within s 262.1(1)` `the signature is printed or otherwise mechanically reproduced on the certificate` `the signature is in accordance with the regulations`

@export If several of us sign separate copies, are they one document (s 262.1(3))?
GIVEN `the document is required or permitted to be signed by more than one individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document one that the Act requires or permits to be executed or signed by more than one individual?
      `it is signed in several documents of like form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it executed or signed in several documents of like form?
      `each of the documents is signed by one or more of the individuals` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is each of the documents signed by one or more of the individuals?
      `the documents are duly signed by all individuals required or permitted to do so` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the documents, taken together, duly signed by all individuals required or permitted to do so?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `If several of us sign separate copies, are they one document` IF
    `the documents are deemed to constitute one document within s 262.1(3)` `the document is required or permitted to be signed by more than one individual` `it is signed in several documents of like form` `each of the documents is signed by one or more of the individuals` `the documents are duly signed by all individuals required or permitted to do so`

@export Must the Director publish a notice that my application was granted (s 262.2)?
GIVEN `the application` IS A `Application whose grant the Director must publish (s 262.2)` @desc Which application was it? (the listed applications under the sections named, or any other application)
      `the Director has made a decision granting the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Director made a decision granting the application?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Director publish a notice that my application was granted` IF
    `the Director must publish a notice of the decision within s 262.2` `the application` `the Director has made a decision granting the application`

-- s 263, 263.1. The annual return is the corporation's duty; the certificates are a claim on the Director.
@export Has the corporation complied with its duty to send the Director an annual return (s 263)?
GIVEN `the corporation has sent the Director an annual return` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation sent the Director an annual return?
      `it is in the form that the Director fixes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it in the form that the Director fixes?
      `it was sent within the period that the Director fixes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it sent within the period that the Director fixes?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the corporation complied with its duty to send the Director an annual return` IF
    `the corporation has complied with the duty to send an annual return within s 263` `the corporation has sent the Director an annual return` `it is in the form that the Director fixes` `it was sent within the period that the Director fixes`

@export May I ask the Director for a certificate of this statement about a corporation (s 263.1(1))?
GIVEN `the statement` IS A `Statement the Director may certify about a corporation (s 263.1(1))` @desc Which statement do you want certified? (that the corporation has sent the Director a required document; that it has paid all required fees; that it exists as of a certain date; or any other statement)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I ask the Director for a certificate of this statement about a corporation` IF
    `the Director may provide any person with a certificate of the statement within s 263.1(1)` `the statement`

@export May the Director refuse me a certificate of existence because the corporation is in default (s 263.1(2))?
GIVEN `the statement` IS A `Statement the Director may certify about a corporation (s 263.1(1))` @desc Which statement do you want certified?
      `the Director knows the corporation is in default of sending a required document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Director know that the corporation is in default of sending a document or other information required to be sent under the Act?
      `the Director knows the corporation is in default of paying a required fee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Director know that the corporation is in default of paying a required fee?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Director refuse me a certificate of existence because the corporation is in default` IF
    `the Director may refuse to issue a certificate of existence within s 263.1(2)` `the statement` `the Director knows the corporation is in default of sending a required document` `the Director knows the corporation is in default of paying a required fee`

-- s 264, 265. Alterations and corrections to what I filed.
@export May the Director alter a document I sent (s 264)?
GIVEN `the document is an affidavit or a statutory declaration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document an affidavit or a statutory declaration?
      `I or my representative authorized the alteration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the alteration authorized by the person who sent the document or by that person's representative?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Director alter a document I sent` IF
    `the Director may alter a notice or document within s 264` `the document is an affidavit or a statutory declaration` `I or my representative authorized the alteration`

@export Must the directors or shareholders pass resolutions to correct an error the Director has pointed out (s 265(1))?
GIVEN `there is an error in articles, a notice, a certificate or other document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there an error in the articles, a notice, a certificate or another document?
      `the Director has requested the correction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Director requested the correction?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the directors or shareholders pass resolutions to correct an error the Director has pointed out` IF
    `the directors or shareholders must pass the resolutions and take the steps within s 265(1)` `there is an error in articles, a notice, a certificate or other document` `the Director has requested the correction`

@export May the Director go ahead with a correction without those resolutions (s 265(2))?
GIVEN `the Director is satisfied that the correction would not prejudice any shareholder or creditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Director satisfied that the correction would not prejudice any of the shareholders or creditors of the corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Director go ahead with a correction without those resolutions` IF
    `the Director may proceed under subsection 265(1) within s 265(2)` `the Director is satisfied that the correction would not prejudice any shareholder or creditor`

@export May the Director accept the correction I have asked for (s 265(3))?
GIVEN `the request is made by the corporation or any other interested person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the request made by the corporation or any other interested person?
      `the correction is approved by the directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the correction approved by the directors of the corporation?
      `the error is obvious` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the error obvious?
      `the error was made by the Director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the error made by the Director?
      `the Director is satisfied that the correction would not prejudice any shareholder or creditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Director satisfied that the correction would not prejudice any of the shareholders or creditors of the corporation?
      `the Director is satisfied that the correction reflects the original intention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Director satisfied that the correction reflects the original intention of the corporation or the incorporators?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Director accept the correction I have asked for` IF
    `the Director may accept the correction within s 265(3)` `the request is made by the corporation or any other interested person` `the correction is approved by the directors` `the error is obvious` `the error was made by the Director` `the Director is satisfied that the correction would not prejudice any shareholder or creditor` `the Director is satisfied that the correction reflects the original intention`

@export May I apply to the court for an order that a document be corrected (s 265(4))?
GIVEN `I think a correction would prejudice shareholders or creditors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In your view, would a correction to any of the documents prejudice any of the shareholders or creditors of the corporation?
      `I am an interested person who wishes a correction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an interested person who wishes a correction?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I apply to the court for an order that a document be corrected` IF
    `the applicant may apply to the court for an order that the document be corrected within s 265(4)` `any person` `I think a correction would prejudice shareholders or creditors` `I am an interested person who wishes a correction`

@export Must I give the Director notice of my application to the court to correct a document (s 265(5))?
GIVEN `I am an applicant under subsection 265(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an applicant to the court for an order that a document be corrected?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I give the Director notice of my application to the court to correct a document` IF
    `the applicant must give the Director notice within s 265(5)` `I am an applicant under subsection 265(4)`

@export Can the Director demand that I surrender the original document when it is corrected (s 265(6))?
GIVEN `a correction is being made under section 265` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a correction being made under the correction section?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Director demand that I surrender the original document when it is corrected` IF
    `the Director may demand the surrender of the original document within s 265(6)` `a correction is being made under section 265`

@export What date does a corrected document bear (s 265(7))?
GIVEN `the date of the document it replaces` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the document that the corrected one replaces?
      `the correction concerns the date of the document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the correction made with respect to the date of the document?
      `the corrected date` IS A DATE @desc What is the corrected date?
      `the court has decided the date the corrected document is to bear` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court decided the date that the corrected document is to bear?
      `the date the court decided` IS A DATE @desc What date has the court decided on? (any date if it has not)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `What date does a corrected document bear` IS
    `the date the corrected document bears within s 265(7)` `the date of the document it replaces` `the correction concerns the date of the document` `the corrected date` courtdate
    WHERE
        courtdate MEANS IF `the court has decided the date the corrected document is to bear` THEN JUST `the date the court decided` ELSE NOTHING

@export Must the Director tell people about a correction that materially changes a certificate (s 265(8))?
GIVEN `a corrected certificate materially amends the terms of the original` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corrected certificate materially amend the terms of the original certificate?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Director tell people about a correction that materially changes a certificate` IF
    `the Director must without delay give notice of the correction within s 265(8)` `a corrected certificate materially amends the terms of the original`

-- s 265.1. Cancellation of articles.
@export May the Director cancel articles and the related certificate (s 265.1(1))?
GIVEN `the circumstances are those prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the circumstances those prescribed by the regulations?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Director cancel articles and the related certificate` IF
    `the Director may cancel the articles and related certificate within s 265.1(1)` `the circumstances are those prescribed`

@export May the Director go ahead with a cancellation without further steps (s 265.1(2))?
GIVEN `the Director is satisfied that the cancellation would not prejudice any shareholder or creditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Director satisfied that the cancellation would not prejudice any of the shareholders or creditors of the corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Director go ahead with a cancellation without further steps` IF
    `the Director may proceed under subsection 265.1(1) within s 265.1(2)` `the Director is satisfied that the cancellation would not prejudice any shareholder or creditor`

@export May the Director cancel articles at my request (s 265.1(3))?
GIVEN `the circumstances are those prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the circumstances those prescribed by the regulations?
      `the request is made by the corporation or any other interested person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the request made by the corporation or any other interested person?
      `the cancellation is approved by the directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the cancellation approved by the directors of the corporation?
      `the Director is satisfied that the cancellation would not prejudice any shareholder or creditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Director satisfied that the cancellation would not prejudice any of the shareholders or creditors of the corporation?
      `the Director is satisfied that the cancellation reflects the original intention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Director satisfied that the cancellation reflects the original intention of the corporation or the incorporators?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Director cancel articles at my request` IF
    `the Director may cancel at the request of the corporation or an interested person within s 265.1(3)` `the circumstances are those prescribed` `the request is made by the corporation or any other interested person` `the cancellation is approved by the directors` `the Director is satisfied that the cancellation would not prejudice any shareholder or creditor` `the Director is satisfied that the cancellation reflects the original intention`

@export May I apply to the court for an order that articles be cancelled (s 265.1(4))?
GIVEN `I think a cancellation would prejudice shareholders or creditors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In your view, would a cancellation of the articles and a related certificate prejudice any of the shareholders or creditors of the corporation?
      `I am an interested person who wishes a cancellation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an interested person who wishes a cancellation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I apply to the court for an order that articles be cancelled` IF
    `the applicant may apply to the court for an order that the articles and certificate be cancelled within s 265.1(4)` `any person` `I think a cancellation would prejudice shareholders or creditors` `I am an interested person who wishes a cancellation`

@export Must I give the Director notice of my application to cancel articles (s 265.1(5))?
GIVEN `I am an applicant under subsection 265.1(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an applicant to the court for an order that the articles and certificate be cancelled?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I give the Director notice of my application to cancel articles` IF
    `the applicant must give the Director notice within s 265.1(5)` `I am an applicant under subsection 265.1(4)`

@export Can the Director demand that I surrender a cancelled certificate (s 265.1(6))?
GIVEN `a certificate has been cancelled under section 265.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a certificate been cancelled under the cancellation section?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Director demand that I surrender a cancelled certificate` IF
    `the Director may demand the surrender of the cancelled certificate within s 265.1(6)` `a certificate has been cancelled under section 265.1`

-- s 266, 266.1. What I may inspect, and what the Director must keep about me.
@export Am I entitled to examine and copy a document the Director holds (s 266(1))?
GIVEN `I have paid the required fee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you paid the required fee?
      `it is during usual business hours` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it during usual business hours?
      `the document is one required to be sent to the Director under the Act or earlier legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document or other information one required to be sent to the Director under the Act, or required to be sent to a person performing a similar function under earlier legislation?
      `it is information sent under section 21.21` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it information sent to the Director under section 21.21 (the register of individuals with significant control)?
      `it is an application under subsection 21.303(3) or a related document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an application under subsection 21.303(3), or a related document?
      `it is a report sent to the Director under subsection 230(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a report sent to the Director by an inspector under the investigation Part (subsection 230(2))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to examine and copy a document the Director holds` IF
    `a person is entitled to examine and make copies or extracts within s 266(1)` `I have paid the required fee` `it is during usual business hours` `the document is one required to be sent to the Director under the Act or earlier legislation` `it is information sent under section 21.21` `it is an application under subsection 21.303(3) or a related document` `it is a report sent to the Director under subsection 230(2)`

@export Must the Director give me a copy or extract I ask for (s 266(2))?
GIVEN `I have asked for a copy, extract, certified copy or certified extract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you asked for a copy, extract, certified copy or certified extract?
      `I may examine the document under subsection 266(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc May you examine the document under the examination section?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Director give me a copy or extract I ask for` IF
    `the Director must provide the copy or extract within s 266(2)` `I have asked for a copy, extract, certified copy or certified extract` `I may examine the document under subsection 266(1)`

@export Is what I tell the Director about wrongdoing a wrongdoing within the Act (s 266.1(3))?
GIVEN `it is a wrongdoing in the ordinary meaning of the word` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a wrongdoing in the ordinary meaning of the word?
      `it is a contravention of any provision of the Act or the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a contravention of any provision of the Act or the regulations?
      `it is the formation of a corporation for a fraudulent or unlawful purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the formation of a corporation for a fraudulent or unlawful purpose?
      `it is a fraudulent or dishonest action of persons concerned with a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a fraudulent or dishonest action of persons concerned with the formation, business or affairs of a corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is what I tell the Director about wrongdoing a wrongdoing within the Act` IF
    `wrongdoing within s 266.1(3)` `it is a wrongdoing in the ordinary meaning of the word` `it is a contravention of any provision of the Act or the regulations` `it is the formation of a corporation for a fraudulent or unlawful purpose` `it is a fraudulent or dishonest action of persons concerned with a corporation`

@export Must the Director keep secret the information I gave about a wrongdoing (s 266.1(1))?
GIVEN `I provided the information on my own initiative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you provide the information on your own initiative?
      `the information relates to a wrongdoing or potential wrongdoing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the information relate to the commission or potential commission of a wrongdoing?
      `the information could reasonably be expected to reveal who I am, or is information I provided in relation to the wrongdoing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Could the information reasonably be expected to reveal your identity, or is it information you provided in relation to the wrongdoing?
      `I consent to its being made available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you consent to its being made available?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Director keep secret the information I gave about a wrongdoing` IF
    `the Director must not make the information available within s 266.1(1)` `I provided the information on my own initiative` `the information relates to a wrongdoing or potential wrongdoing` `the information could reasonably be expected to reveal who I am, or is information I provided in relation to the wrongdoing` `I consent to its being made available`

@export May the Director pass the information I gave on to this recipient (s 266.1(2))?
GIVEN `the recipient` IS A `Recipient of protected information (s 266.1(2))` @desc Who is the recipient? (an investigative body referred to in the section on investigative bodies, the Financial Transactions and Reports Analysis Centre of Canada, a prescribed entity, or anyone else)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Director pass the information I gave on to this recipient` IF
    `the Director may provide the information to the recipient within s 266.1(2)` `the recipient`

-- s 267, 267.1.
@export Must the Director keep the document I sent (s 267(1))?
GIVEN `the document was received and accepted by the Director, or by a person performing a similar function under earlier legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the document received and accepted by the Director under the Act, or by a person performing a similar function under earlier legislation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Director keep the document I sent` IF
    `the Director must keep the document within s 267(1)` `the document was received and accepted by the Director, or by a person performing a similar function under earlier legislation`

@export If the Director keeps documents electronically, must I be given a copy in readable form (s 267(2)(a))?
GIVEN `documents are kept by the Director otherwise than in written form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the documents kept by the Director otherwise than in written form?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `If the Director keeps documents electronically, must I be given a copy in readable form` IF
    `the Director must furnish a copy in intelligible form within s 267(2)(a)` `documents are kept by the Director otherwise than in written form`

@export Is a report reproduced from the Director's electronic records admissible in evidence (s 267(2)(b))?
GIVEN `documents are kept by the Director otherwise than in written form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the documents kept by the Director otherwise than in written form?
      `it is a report reproduced from those documents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a report reproduced from those documents?
      `it is certified by the Director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it certified by the Director?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a report reproduced from the Director's electronic records admissible in evidence` IF
    `the report is admissible in evidence to the same extent as the originals within s 267(2)(b)` `documents are kept by the Director otherwise than in written form` `it is a report reproduced from those documents` `it is certified by the Director`

@export Is the Director still required to keep or produce this document (s 267(3))?
GIVEN `it is a certificate with attached articles or statement received under section 262, or another prescribed document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a certificate with any attached articles or statement received under the sending-of-articles section, or another prescribed document or class of documents?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc As of what day are you asking?
      `the last day of the period prescribed for keeping or producing it` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the period prescribed for keeping or producing the document?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the Director still required to keep or produce this document` IF
    `the Director is required to keep or produce the document within s 267(3)` `it is a certificate with attached articles or statement received under section 262, or another prescribed document` `the day I am asking about` `the last day of the period prescribed for keeping or producing it`

@export May the Director make documents available by an electronic system (s 267.1)?
GIVEN `the system or device is a system of mechanical or electronic data processing or another information storage device` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the system or device a system of mechanical or electronic data processing, or another information storage device?
      `it can reproduce the information or notice in intelligible form within a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it capable of reproducing any required information or notice in intelligible form within a reasonable time?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Director make documents available by an electronic system` IF
    `information or notices may be made available or published by the system or device within s 267.1` `the system or device is a system of mechanical or electronic data processing or another information storage device` `it can reproduce the information or notice in intelligible form within a reasonable time`

§§ `Bodies incorporated under other Acts of Parliament (s 268)`

-- s 268(1), (4.2). What counts as the body's "charter", and when a body is deemed to be an Act-of-Parliament body.
@export Is this document my body corporate's charter (s 268(1))?
GIVEN `it is a charter in the ordinary meaning of the word` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a charter in the ordinary meaning of the word?
      `it is an act of incorporation or an amendment to it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an act of incorporation, or an amendment to one?
      `it is letters patent of incorporation or letters patent supplementary to them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it letters patent of incorporation, or letters patent supplementary to them?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this document my body corporate's charter` IF
    `charter within s 268(1)` `it is a charter in the ordinary meaning of the word` `it is an act of incorporation or an amendment to it` `it is letters patent of incorporation or letters patent supplementary to them`

@export Is my body corporate treated as incorporated under an Act of Parliament other than this Act or a special Act (s 268(4.2))?
GIVEN `my body corporate is incorporated or continued under an Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your body corporate incorporated or continued under an Act of Parliament?
      `the Bank Act applies to it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Bank Act apply to it?
      `the Cooperative Credit Associations Act applies to it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Cooperative Credit Associations Act apply to it?
      `the Insurance Companies Act applies to it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Insurance Companies Act apply to it?
      `the Trust and Loan Companies Act applies to it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Trust and Loan Companies Act apply to it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my body corporate treated as incorporated under an Act of Parliament other than this Act or a special Act` IF
    `the body corporate is deemed to be incorporated or continued by or under an Act of Parliament other than this Act or a special Act within s 268(4.2)` `my body corporate is incorporated or continued under an Act of Parliament` `the Bank Act applies to it` `the Cooperative Credit Associations Act applies to it` `the Insurance Companies Act applies to it` `the Trust and Loan Companies Act applies to it`

-- s 268(2), (2.1), (3). Amending the charter on a continuance, by special resolution, despite the charter.
@export Can the shareholders of my special-Act body corporate amend its charter by special resolution on a continuance (s 268(2))?
GIVEN `it is in connection with a continuance under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the amendment made in connection with a continuance under the Act?
      `my body corporate is incorporated or continued under a special Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your body corporate incorporated or continued by or under a special Act of Parliament?
      `the shareholders are entitled to vote at annual meetings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shareholders entitled to vote at annual meetings of shareholders?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the shareholders of my special-Act body corporate amend its charter by special resolution on a continuance` IF
    `the shareholders may authorize the directors and amend the charter by special resolution despite the charter within s 268(2)` `it is in connection with a continuance under this Act` `my body corporate is incorporated or continued under a special Act of Parliament` `the shareholders are entitled to vote at annual meetings`

@export Can the shareholders of my other-Act body corporate amend its charter by special resolution on a continuance (s 268(2.1))?
GIVEN `it is in connection with a continuance under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the amendment made in connection with a continuance under the Act?
      `my body corporate is incorporated or continued under another Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your body corporate incorporated or continued by or under an Act of Parliament other than the Act and other than a special Act?
      `the shareholders are entitled to vote at annual meetings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shareholders entitled to vote at annual meetings of shareholders?
      `another Act or the charter forbids it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does another Act of Parliament or the charter of the body corporate forbid it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the shareholders of my other-Act body corporate amend its charter by special resolution on a continuance` IF
    `the shareholders may authorize the directors and amend the charter by special resolution subject to any other Act and the charter within s 268(2.1)` `it is in connection with a continuance under this Act` `my body corporate is incorporated or continued under another Act of Parliament` `the shareholders are entitled to vote at annual meetings` `another Act or the charter forbids it`

@export Can the shareholders make this change to a class or series of shares by special resolution on a continuance (s 268(3))?
GIVEN `the change is of the nature referred to in subsection 176(1) and affects a class or series of shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the change of a nature referred to in the section on class votes on amendments (subsection 176(1)), and does it affect a class or series of shares?
      `the change is of the nature in paragraph 176(1)(a), (b) or (e)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the change of a nature referred to in paragraph 176(1)(a), (b) or (e)?
      `the charter otherwise provides` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the charter of the body corporate otherwise provide in respect of an amendment of that nature?
      `the holders of the class or series approve it under section 176` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the holders of the class or series of shares approve the change in accordance with section 176?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the shareholders make this change to a class or series of shares by special resolution on a continuance` IF
    `the shareholders may make the change by special resolution under subsection 268(2) or (2.1) within s 268(3)` `the change is of the nature referred to in subsection 176(1) and affects a class or series of shares` `the change is of the nature in paragraph 176(1)(a), (b) or (e)` `the charter otherwise provides` `the holders of the class or series approve it under section 176`

-- s 268(4), (4.1). The directors' power.
@export Can the directors of my special-Act body corporate apply for a certificate of continuance despite the charter (s 268(4))?
GIVEN `my body corporate is incorporated or continued under a special Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your body corporate incorporated or continued by or under a special Act of Parliament?
      `the articles of continuance make no amendment other than one required to conform to the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the articles of continuance make no amendment to the charter other than one required to conform to the Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the directors of my special-Act body corporate apply for a certificate of continuance despite the charter` IF
    `the directors may apply for a certificate of continuance despite the charter within s 268(4)` `my body corporate is incorporated or continued under a special Act of Parliament` `the articles of continuance make no amendment other than one required to conform to the Act`

@export Can the directors of my other-Act body corporate apply for a certificate of continuance (s 268(4.1))?
GIVEN `my body corporate is incorporated or continued under another Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your body corporate incorporated or continued by or under an Act of Parliament other than the Act and other than a special Act?
      `the articles of continuance make no amendment other than one required to conform to the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the articles of continuance make no amendment to the charter other than one required to conform to the Act?
      `another Act or the charter forbids it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does another Act of Parliament or the charter of the body corporate forbid it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the directors of my other-Act body corporate apply for a certificate of continuance` IF
    `the directors may apply for a certificate of continuance subject to any other Act and the charter within s 268(4.1)` `my body corporate is incorporated or continued under another Act of Parliament` `the articles of continuance make no amendment other than one required to conform to the Act` `another Act or the charter forbids it`

@export Am I barred from dissenting under section 190 from an amendment made on a continuance under section 268 (s 268(5))?
GIVEN `the amendment is made under subsection 268(2), (2.1), (3), (4) or (4.1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the amendment made under one of the powers to amend on a continuance (subsections 268(2), (2.1), (3), (4) or (4.1))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I barred from dissenting under section 190 from an amendment made on a continuance under section 268` IF
    `a shareholder is not entitled to dissent under section 190 within s 268(5)` `the amendment is made under subsection 268(2), (2.1), (3), (4) or (4.1)`

-- s 268(6), (9). The Governor in Council's power over the body, and the consequence of not applying.
@export Can the Governor in Council require my body corporate to apply for a certificate of continuance (s 268(6))?
GIVEN `my body corporate is incorporated under an Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your body corporate incorporated by or under an Act of Parliament?
      `the Canada Not-for-profit Corporations Act applies to it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Canada Not-for-profit Corporations Act apply to it?
      `it is a bank` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a bank?
      `it is an association to which the Cooperative Credit Associations Act applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an association to which the Cooperative Credit Associations Act applies?
      `it is a company or society to which the Insurance Companies Act applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a company or society to which the Insurance Companies Act applies?
      `it is a company to which the Trust and Loan Companies Act applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a company to which the Trust and Loan Companies Act applies?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Governor in Council require my body corporate to apply for a certificate of continuance` IF
    `the Governor in Council may require the body corporate to apply for a certificate of continuance within s 268(6)` `my body corporate is incorporated under an Act of Parliament` `the Canada Not-for-profit Corporations Act applies to it` `it is a bank` `it is an association to which the Cooperative Credit Associations Act applies` `it is a company or society to which the Insurance Companies Act applies` `it is a company to which the Trust and Loan Companies Act applies`

@export Is my body corporate dissolved because it did not apply for continuance in time (s 268(9))?
GIVEN `my body corporate is one that was required to apply by order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your body corporate required by order to apply for a certificate of continuance?
      `it applied within the period prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it applied to obtain a certificate of continuance within the period prescribed?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc As of what day are you asking?
      `the last day of the period prescribed` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the period prescribed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my body corporate dissolved because it did not apply for continuance in time` IF
    `the body corporate is dissolved on the expiration of the period within s 268(9)` `my body corporate is one that was required to apply by order` `it applied within the period prescribed` `the day I am asking about` `the last day of the period prescribed`

-- s 268(8), (8.1).
@export Does my body corporate escape the continuance fees (s 268(8))?
GIVEN `my body corporate obtains a certificate of continuance under section 268` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your body corporate obtain a certificate of continuance under section 268?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my body corporate escape the continuance fees` IF
    `the body corporate is not required to pay the fees otherwise payable for the continuance within s 268(8)` `my body corporate obtains a certificate of continuance under section 268`

@export Does the special Act stop applying to my body corporate once it is continued (s 268(8.1))?
GIVEN `my body corporate was incorporated by a special Act and is continued as a corporation under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your body corporate incorporated by a special Act of Parliament, and is it continued as a corporation under the Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the special Act stop applying to my body corporate once it is continued` IF
    `the special Act ceases to apply to the corporation within s 268(8.1)` `my body corporate was incorporated by a special Act and is continued as a corporation under the Act`

-- s 268(10), (11).
@export May my body corporate apply for a certificate of continuance under the Act (s 268(10), (11))?
GIVEN `the Canada Not-for-profit Corporations Act applies to it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Canada Not-for-profit Corporations Act apply to your body corporate?
      `it is a similar body corporate incorporated otherwise than by or under an Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a similar body corporate incorporated otherwise than by or under an Act of Parliament?
      `it is incorporated by or under a Special Act as defined in the Canada Transportation Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it incorporated by or under a Special Act as defined in section 87 of the Canada Transportation Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my body corporate apply for a certificate of continuance under the Act` IF
    `the body corporate may apply for a certificate of continuance within s 268(10) and s 268(11)` barred excepted
    WHERE
        barred MEANS `the body corporate may not apply for a certificate of continuance under section 187 within s 268(10)` `the Canada Not-for-profit Corporations Act applies to it` `it is a similar body corporate incorporated otherwise than by or under an Act of Parliament`
        excepted MEANS `the body corporate may apply for a certificate of continuance under section 187 within s 268(11)` `it is incorporated by or under a Special Act as defined in the Canada Transportation Act`

§§ `The Schedule`

-- The Schedule, referred to in s 21.31 (another piece's), lists the offences whose disclosure the Director may
-- make to the investigative bodies; this question asks only whether an offence is on the list.
@export Is the offence in question one the Schedule lists?
GIVEN `the Act the offence is under` IS A `Act the Schedule lists offences under` @desc Under which Act is the offence? (one of the eight Acts the Schedule names, or any other Act)
      `the section of the Act the offence is under` IS A STRING @desc Which section is the offence under? (for example 380, or 124.2)
      `the subsection the offence is under, or empty` IS A STRING @desc Which subsection is it under? (leave empty if none)
      `the section contravened, or empty` IS A STRING @desc For an offence of contravening some other section, which section is contravened? (leave empty if none)
      `the offence is under an Act of Parliament or a provincial law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence under an Act of Parliament or a law of the legislature of a province?
      `that Act or law provides for the imposition of a tax or duty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that Act or law provide for the imposition of a tax or duty?
      `the maximum term of imprisonment in years` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum term of imprisonment for the offence, in years?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the offence in question one the Schedule lists` IF
    `an offence is in the Schedule` `the Act the offence is under` `the section of the Act the offence is under` `the subsection the offence is under, or empty` `the section contravened, or empty` item9
    WHERE
        item9 MEANS `an offence is within item 9 of the Schedule` `the offence is under an Act of Parliament or a provincial law` `that Act or law provides for the imposition of a tax or duty` `the maximum term of imprisonment in years`

§§ `Related provisions`

-- S.C. 2001, c. 14, s. 233 appears above, with the apportionment Part. The remaining transitional provisions that a
-- shareholder or director of an existing corporation might ask about follow.
@export Is my proceeding that began before the 1985 amendments continued under the amended provisions (R.S. 1985, c. 27 (2nd Supp.), s. 11)?
GIVEN `the day my proceeding was commenced` IS A DATE @desc On what day was your proceeding commenced?
      `the day section 10 of R.S. 1985, c. 27 (2nd Supp.) came into force` IS A DATE @desc On what day did section 10 of the 1985 amending Act (R.S. 1985, c. 27 (2nd Supp.)) come into force?
      `a provision amended by that Act applies to my proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a provision amended by the schedule to that Act apply to your proceeding?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my proceeding that began before the 1985 amendments continued under the amended provisions` IF
    `the proceeding is continued in accordance with the amended provisions within R.S. 1985, c. 27 (2nd Supp.), s. 11` `the day my proceeding was commenced` `the day section 10 of R.S. 1985, c. 27 (2nd Supp.) came into force` `a provision amended by that Act applies to my proceeding`

@export Is my proceeding that began before the 1990 amendments taken up under the amended provision (S.C. 1990, c. 17, s. 45(1))?
GIVEN `the day my proceeding was commenced` IS A DATE @desc On what day was your proceeding commenced?
      `the day subsection 45(1) of S.C. 1990, c. 17 came into force` IS A DATE @desc On what day did subsection 45(1) of S.C. 1990, c. 17 come into force?
      `a provision amended by that Act applies to my proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a provision amended by that Act apply to your proceeding?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my proceeding that began before the 1990 amendments taken up under the amended provision` IF
    `the proceeding is taken up and continued under the amended provision within S.C. 1990, c. 17, s. 45(1)` `the day my proceeding was commenced` `the day subsection 45(1) of S.C. 1990, c. 17 came into force` `a provision amended by that Act applies to my proceeding`

@export Is my proceeding that began before the 1998 amendments taken up under the amended provision (S.C. 1998, c. 30, s. 10)?
GIVEN `the day my proceeding was commenced` IS A DATE @desc On what day was your proceeding commenced?
      `the day section 10 of S.C. 1998, c. 30 came into force` IS A DATE @desc On what day did section 10 of S.C. 1998, c. 30 come into force?
      `a provision amended by sections 12 to 16 of that Act applies to my proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a provision amended by sections 12 to 16 of that Act apply to your proceeding?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my proceeding that began before the 1998 amendments taken up under the amended provision` IF
    `the proceeding is taken up and continued under the amended provision within S.C. 1998, c. 30, s. 10` `the day my proceeding was commenced` `the day section 10 of S.C. 1998, c. 30 came into force` `a provision amended by sections 12 to 16 of that Act applies to my proceeding`

@export Does the 1994 amendment to subsection 125(1) apply to this year (S.C. 1994, c. 21, s. 125(2))?
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER @desc Which year are you asking about? (for example 1989)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the 1994 amendment to subsection 125(1) apply to this year` IF
    `subsection 125(1) applies to the year within S.C. 1994, c. 21, s. 125(2)` `the year`

@export Was the continuance of my railway company before 1996 valid despite its being incorporated under an Act of Parliament (S.C. 1996, c. 10, s. 214)?
GIVEN `the continuance was of a railway company and was granted under section 187` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the continuance of a railway company, and was it granted under the continuance section (section 187)?
      `the day the continuance was granted` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the continuance granted?
      `the day section 212 of S.C. 1996, c. 10 came into force` IS A DATE @desc On what day did section 212 of S.C. 1996, c. 10 come into force?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was the continuance of my railway company before 1996 valid despite its being incorporated under an Act of Parliament` IF
    `the continuance is not invalid because the company was incorporated by or under an Act of Parliament within S.C. 1996, c. 10, s. 214` `the continuance was of a railway company and was granted under section 187` `the day the continuance was granted` `the day section 212 of S.C. 1996, c. 10 came into force`

@export By what day must my body corporate apply for continuance (S.C. 2009, c. 23, s. 297(6))?
GIVEN `the day subsection 297(6) of S.C. 2009, c. 23 came into force` IS A DATE @desc On what day did subsection 297(6) of S.C. 2009, c. 23 come into force?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must my body corporate apply for continuance` IS
    `the last day to apply for continuance within S.C. 2009, c. 23, s. 297(6)` `the day subsection 297(6) of S.C. 2009, c. 23 came into force`

@export Is my body corporate dissolved because it did not apply for continuance in the six months (S.C. 2009, c. 23, s. 297(6))?
GIVEN `my body corporate is one referred to in subsection 297(2) of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your body corporate one referred to in subsection 297(2) of S.C. 2009, c. 23?
      `the day subsection 297(6) of S.C. 2009, c. 23 came into force` IS A DATE @desc On what day did subsection 297(6) of S.C. 2009, c. 23 come into force?
      `it applied for a certificate of continuance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your body corporate apply for a certificate of continuance under section 187?
      `the day it applied` IS A DATE @desc On what day did it apply? (any date if it did not)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc As of what day are you asking?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my body corporate dissolved because it did not apply for continuance in the six months` IF
    `the body corporate is dissolved on the expiry of the period within S.C. 2009, c. 23, s. 297(6)` `my body corporate is one referred to in subsection 297(2) of that Act` `the day subsection 297(6) of S.C. 2009, c. 23 came into force` applied `the day I am asking about`
    WHERE
        applied MEANS IF `it applied for a certificate of continuance` THEN JUST `the day it applied` ELSE NOTHING

